window.I13_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","cards":[{"w":"evolution","p":"n.","d":"slow change in living things over many generations","c":"演化","s":"Our biology teacher showed us fossils of early horses, and she explained how evolution slowly changed their size and teeth over millions of years.","t":"我們的生物老師給我們看早期馬的化石，並解釋了演化如何在數百萬年間慢慢改變牠們的體型和牙齒。"},{"w":"natural selection","p":"n.phr.","d":"process where living things best suited to their surroundings survive","c":"天擇","s":"Rabbits with white fur are harder for foxes to see in the snow, so natural selection helps them survive and pass on that colour.","t":"白色毛皮的兔子在雪地裡較不容易被狐狸看見，所以天擇幫助牠們存活並把這種毛色傳下去。"},{"w":"sexual selection","p":"n.phr.","d":"choosing mates by features such as bright colours or songs","c":"性擇","s":"Female birds often choose males with the brightest feathers, and scientists believe sexual selection explains why many male birds look so colourful.","t":"雌鳥常常選擇羽毛最鮮豔的雄鳥，而科學家相信性擇解釋了為什麼許多雄鳥看起來如此色彩繽紛。"},{"w":"artificial selection","p":"n.phr.","d":"when humans choose which plants or animals breed","c":"人擇；人工選擇","s":"All the different dog breeds came from wolves, but they look so different because people used artificial selection for thousands of years.","t":"所有不同的狗品種都來自狼，但牠們看起來如此不同，是因為人們數千年來一直進行人擇。"},{"w":"fitness","p":"n.","d":"how well a living thing survives and has young","c":"適存度","s":"In biology, fitness does not mean going to the gym, because it describes how many healthy young an animal can produce.","t":"在生物學中，適存度並不是指去健身房，因為它描述的是一隻動物能產下多少健康的後代。"},{"w":"common ancestor","p":"n.phr.","d":"an earlier species that two later species both came from","c":"共同祖先","s":"Humans and chimpanzees look different today, but scientists say we shared a common ancestor that lived about six million years ago.","t":"人類和黑猩猩今天看起來不同，但科學家說我們有一個大約生活在六百萬年前的共同祖先。"},{"w":"speciation","p":"n.","d":"the forming of a new and separate species","c":"物種形成","s":"When a river split one group of beetles into two, the groups stopped meeting, and over time speciation produced two different kinds.","t":"當一條河把一群甲蟲分成兩群後，兩群不再相遇，經過一段時間，物種形成產生了兩種不同的甲蟲。"},{"w":"descent","p":"n.","d":"coming from earlier family members or species","c":"血統；由來","s":"The museum guide explained that whales are of land-animal descent, and the small bones in their bodies are clues to that past.","t":"博物館導覽員解釋說鯨魚是陸地動物血統，而牠們體內的小骨頭就是那段過去的線索。"},{"w":"vestigial","p":"adj.","d":"still present in the body but no longer useful","c":"退化的；殘留的","s":"Some snakes still have tiny vestigial leg bones inside their bodies, although they have not used legs for millions of years.","t":"有些蛇的體內仍有微小的退化的腿骨，雖然牠們已經數百萬年沒有使用腿了。"},{"w":"missing link","p":"n.phr.","d":"a fossil that connects two groups of living things","c":"缺失的環節","s":"Newspapers called the feathered dinosaur fossil a missing link, because it seemed to connect reptiles and modern birds.","t":"報紙把這個有羽毛的恐龍化石稱為缺失的環節，因為它似乎連接了爬行動物和現代鳥類。"},{"w":"tree of life","p":"n.phr.","d":"a diagram showing how all living things are related","c":"生命之樹","s":"The poster in the science lab shows a huge tree of life, and students can trace how fish, birds and humans are related.","t":"科學實驗室裡的海報展示了一棵巨大的生命之樹，學生可以追溯魚類、鳥類和人類之間的關係。"},{"w":"coevolution","p":"n.","d":"when two species change over time because of each other","c":"共同演化","s":"Some flowers have long tubes and some moths have long tongues, and scientists see this as a clear example of coevolution.","t":"有些花有長長的花管，而有些蛾有長長的口器，科學家把這視為共同演化的清楚例子。"},{"w":"convergent evolution","p":"n.phr.","d":"when unrelated animals develop similar features","c":"趨同演化","s":"Sharks and dolphins are not closely related, but they both have smooth bodies and fins because of convergent evolution.","t":"鯊魚和海豚並不是近親，但因為趨同演化，牠們都有光滑的身體和鰭。"},{"w":"arms race","p":"n.phr.","d":"a contest where each side keeps improving to beat the other","c":"軍備競賽","s":"Cheetahs became faster to catch gazelles, while gazelles became faster to escape, so the two animals are locked in an arms race.","t":"獵豹變得更快以捕捉瞪羚，而瞪羚也變得更快以逃脫，所以這兩種動物陷入了一場軍備競賽。"},{"w":"selection pressure","p":"n.phr.","d":"a force in nature that affects which animals survive","c":"選擇壓力","s":"When the winters became colder, there was strong selection pressure on the deer, and only those with thick coats survived.","t":"當冬天變得更冷時，鹿群受到強大的選擇壓力，只有毛皮厚的鹿才存活下來。"},{"w":"advantageous","p":"adj.","d":"helpful and giving a better chance of success","c":"有利的","s":"Long necks were advantageous for giraffes because they could reach leaves high in the trees, so more long-necked giraffes survived.","t":"長脖子對長頸鹿是有利的，因為牠們能吃到樹上高處的葉子，所以有更多長脖子的長頸鹿存活下來。"},{"w":"outcompete","p":"v.","d":"to do better than others in getting food or space","c":"競爭勝過","s":"Grey squirrels were brought to Britain from America, and they outcompete the native red squirrels in many forests.","t":"灰松鼠從美洲被帶到英國，而牠們在許多森林中競爭勝過了本地的紅松鼠。"},{"w":"finch","p":"n.","d":"a small bird with a short, strong beak","c":"雀鳥","s":"Darwin studied the different finch on the Galápagos Islands, and he noticed that their beaks matched the food on each island.","t":"達爾文研究了加拉巴哥群島上不同的雀鳥，並注意到牠們的喙與每個島上的食物相符。"},{"w":"beak","p":"n.","d":"the hard, pointed mouth of a bird","c":"鳥喙","s":"Birds that crack hard seeds usually have a thick beak, but birds that catch insects often have a thin one.","t":"會咬開堅硬種子的鳥通常有厚實的鳥喙，但捕捉昆蟲的鳥通常有細長的喙。"},{"w":"primordial","p":"adj.","d":"existing at the very beginning of time","c":"原始的；最初的","s":"Some scientists think life began in a primordial soup of chemicals in the ocean, but others believe it started near hot vents.","t":"有些科學家認為生命起源於海洋中化學物質組成的原始的湯，但其他人相信生命始於熱泉噴口附近。"},{"w":"single-celled","p":"adj.","d":"made of only one cell","c":"單細胞的","s":"The first living things on Earth were tiny single-celled creatures, and they existed alone for billions of years before animals appeared.","t":"地球上最早的生物是微小的單細胞的生物，而牠們在動物出現之前獨自存在了數十億年。"},{"w":"multicellular","p":"adj.","d":"made of many cells working together","c":"多細胞的","s":"Plants and animals are multicellular living things, but bacteria are made of just one cell each.","t":"植物和動物都是多細胞的生物，但細菌每個都只由一個細胞組成。"},{"w":"microorganism","p":"n.","d":"a living thing too small to see without a microscope","c":"微生物","s":"A spoonful of garden soil contains millions of microorganism, and many of them help plants grow by breaking down dead leaves.","t":"一湯匙的花園土壤含有數百萬個微生物，而且其中許多會分解枯葉來幫助植物生長。"},{"w":"naturalist","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies plants and animals in nature","c":"博物學家","s":"As a young naturalist, Darwin collected beetles and birds, and his notes later helped him form his famous theory.","t":"年輕時身為博物學家的達爾文收集甲蟲和鳥類，而他的筆記後來幫助他形成了著名的理論。"},{"w":"biologist","p":"n.","d":"a scientist who studies living things","c":"生物學家","s":"My cousin works as a biologist in Taiwan, and she spends weeks in the mountains counting frogs and taking photos.","t":"我的表姐在台灣擔任生物學家，她會花好幾週在山裡數青蛙和拍照。"},{"w":"variant","p":"n.","d":"a form of something that is slightly different","c":"變種；變體","s":"Doctors watched the new variant of the virus closely, because it spread faster than the earlier type.","t":"醫生密切觀察這種病毒的新變種，因為它比較早的類型傳播得更快。"},{"w":"ancestral","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to earlier family members or species","c":"祖先的","s":"Scientists studied the ancestral home of the first dogs, and they found that wolves there lived close to early humans.","t":"科學家研究了最早的狗的祖先的家園，並發現那裡的狼和早期人類生活得很近。"},{"w":"taxonomy","p":"n.","d":"the science of naming and grouping living things","c":"分類學","s":"Students learn taxonomy in their first year, so they can name animals correctly and know which group each one belongs to.","t":"學生在第一年學習分類學，好讓他們能正確地為動物命名並知道每種動物屬於哪一類。"},{"w":"peppered moth","p":"n.phr.","d":"a moth that changed colour when cities became sooty","c":"樺尺蛾","s":"During the Industrial Revolution, dark peppered moth became more common, because they were hidden on dirty black trees.","t":"在工業革命期間，深色的樺尺蛾變得更常見，因為牠們能隱藏在骯髒的黑色樹幹上。"},{"w":"superbug","p":"n.","d":"a germ that common medicines can no longer kill","c":"超級細菌","s":"Doctors warn that taking medicine you do not need can create a superbug, and then ordinary drugs will stop working.","t":"醫生警告服用不需要的藥物可能會產生超級細菌，然後一般的藥物就會失效。"},{"w":"drug-resistant","p":"adj.","d":"not affected by medicines that once worked","c":"抗藥性的","s":"The hospital found a drug-resistant infection in one patient, so the nurses moved him to a separate room.","t":"醫院在一名病人身上發現了抗藥性的感染，所以護理師把他移到單獨的病房。"},{"w":"giraffe","p":"n.","d":"a tall African animal with a very long neck","c":"長頸鹿","s":"Male giraffe swing their long necks at each other when they fight, and the stronger one usually wins a partner.","t":"雄長頸鹿打鬥時會互相揮動長脖子，而較強壯的那一隻通常會贏得伴侶。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","cards":[{"w":"hominid","p":"n.","d":"a member of the group including humans and great apes","c":"人科動物","s":"The team discovered the teeth of an early hominid in a cave, and they believe it lived about two million years ago.","t":"研究團隊在一個洞穴中發現了一個早期人科動物的牙齒，他們相信牠生活在大約兩百萬年前。"},{"w":"Homo sapiens","p":"n.","d":"the scientific name for modern humans","c":"智人","s":"Homo sapiens first appeared in Africa, and over thousands of years our species spread to every continent.","t":"智人最早出現在非洲，而經過數千年，我們這個物種擴散到了每一個大陸。"},{"w":"Neanderthal","p":"n.","d":"an early human who lived in Europe and Asia","c":"尼安德塔人","s":"Many people today carry a little Neanderthal DNA, because our ancestors met and had children with them long ago.","t":"現今許多人身上帶有一點尼安德塔人的DNA，因為我們的祖先很久以前曾與他們相遇並生下孩子。"},{"w":"great ape","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large primate such as a gorilla or chimpanzee","c":"大型猿類","s":"The zoo built a large forest area for every great ape, because these clever animals need space to climb and explore.","t":"動物園為每一隻大型猿類建造了大片森林區，因為這些聰明的動物需要空間攀爬和探索。"},{"w":"chimpanzee","p":"n.","d":"an African ape that is closely related to humans","c":"黑猩猩","s":"Jane Goodall watched a chimpanzee use a stick to catch termites, and this showed that animals can make tools too.","t":"珍古德看見一隻黑猩猩用樹枝捕捉白蟻，而這顯示動物也會製作工具。"},{"w":"gorilla","p":"n.","d":"the largest ape, living in African forests","c":"大猩猩","s":"The silverback gorilla looked scary, but he was very gentle with the babies in his family.","t":"那隻銀背大猩猩看起來很可怕，但他對家族裡的寶寶非常溫柔。"},{"w":"orangutan","p":"n.","d":"a red-haired ape from Borneo and Sumatra","c":"紅毛猩猩","s":"The young orangutan stays with its mother for about eight years, and she teaches it which fruits are safe to eat.","t":"年幼的紅毛猩猩會和媽媽待在一起大約八年，而媽媽會教牠哪些水果可以安全食用。"},{"w":"bonobo","p":"n.","d":"a peaceful ape closely related to the chimpanzee","c":"巴諾布猿","s":"A bonobo group usually solves fights by sharing food and hugging, so scientists call them the peaceful apes.","t":"巴諾布猿群體通常以分享食物和擁抱來解決爭吵，所以科學家稱牠們為和平的猿類。"},{"w":"bipedal","p":"adj.","d":"walking on two legs","c":"雙足行走的","s":"Our early ancestors became bipedal on the open grasslands, and walking upright left their hands free to carry food.","t":"我們早期的祖先在開闊的草原上變成雙足行走的，而直立行走讓他們的雙手能空出來搬運食物。"},{"w":"upright","p":"adj.","d":"standing straight up","c":"直立的","s":"Bears can stand upright for a short time, but they usually walk on four legs when they look for food.","t":"熊可以短時間直立站著，但牠們找食物時通常用四條腿走路。"},{"w":"posture","p":"n.","d":"the way you hold your body","c":"姿勢","s":"Sitting at a desk for hours is bad for your posture, and doctors say our spines evolved for walking, not sitting.","t":"在書桌前坐好幾個小時對你的姿勢不好，醫生說我們的脊椎是為了走路而演化的，而不是為了坐著。"},{"w":"opposable thumb","p":"n.phr.","d":"a thumb that can touch the other fingers","c":"可對握的拇指","s":"We can hold a pencil and open a jar easily, because we have an opposable thumb that works with our other fingers.","t":"我們能輕鬆握筆和打開罐子，因為我們有一根能與其他手指配合的可對握的拇指。"},{"w":"toolmaking","p":"n.","d":"the activity of making tools","c":"工具製作","s":"Early toolmaking began with simple sharp stones, but over time people learned to make spears, needles and fishing hooks.","t":"早期的工具製作從簡單的尖銳石頭開始，但隨著時間推移，人們學會了製作矛、針和魚鉤。"},{"w":"early humans","p":"n.phr.","d":"people who lived very long ago","c":"早期人類","s":"early humans learned to control fire, and cooking their food gave them more energy for their growing brains.","t":"早期人類學會了控制火，而烹煮食物讓他們有更多能量供應逐漸變大的大腦。"},{"w":"interbreed","p":"v.","d":"to produce young with a different group or species","c":"雜交繁殖","s":"Modern humans and Neanderthals interbred in the past, so traces of their DNA still exist in many people today.","t":"現代人類和尼安德塔人過去曾雜交繁殖，所以他們DNA的痕跡至今仍存在於許多人身上。"},{"w":"skeletal","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the bones of a body","c":"骨骼的","s":"The doctor studied the skeletal remains carefully, and she found that the person had walked long distances every day.","t":"這位醫生仔細研究了這些骨骼的遺骸，並發現這個人生前每天都走很長的路。"},{"w":"jawbone","p":"n.","d":"the bone that holds the lower teeth","c":"顎骨","s":"The ancient jawbone was small and had worn teeth, so scientists guessed the person ate tough plants.","t":"這塊古老的顎骨很小，牙齒也磨損了，所以科學家推測這個人吃的是堅韌的植物。"},{"w":"spine","p":"n.","d":"the row of bones down the middle of your back","c":"脊椎","s":"Our spine has an S-shape that helps us walk on two legs, but it also explains why so many adults get back pain.","t":"我們的脊椎呈S形，幫助我們用雙腿走路，但這也解釋了為什麼這麼多成年人會背痛。"},{"w":"primatologist","p":"n.","d":"a scientist who studies monkeys and apes","c":"靈長類動物學家","s":"The primatologist lived in the rainforest for two years, and she learned to recognise every monkey by its face.","t":"那位靈長類動物學家在雨林裡住了兩年，而她學會了從臉認出每一隻猴子。"},{"w":"anthropologist","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies human societies and cultures","c":"人類學家","s":"An anthropologist visited the mountain village to study its traditions, and the villagers taught her their old songs.","t":"一位人類學家到山村研究當地的傳統，而村民教她唱他們古老的歌謠。"},{"w":"anthropology","p":"n.","d":"the study of humans, their history and culture","c":"人類學","s":"My sister is studying anthropology at university, because she wants to understand how people lived thousands of years ago.","t":"我姐姐在大學主修人類學，因為她想了解人們數千年前是如何生活的。"},{"w":"body hair","p":"n.phr.","d":"the hair that grows on the body","c":"體毛","s":"Humans lost most of their body hair over time, and some scientists think this helped them stay cool while running.","t":"人類隨著時間失去了大部分的體毛，而有些科學家認為這幫助他們在奔跑時保持涼爽。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","cards":[{"w":"cell","p":"n.","d":"the smallest living unit of a plant or animal","c":"細胞","s":"Every cell in your body contains instructions, and these instructions tell it whether to become skin, bone or blood.","t":"你身體裡的每一個細胞都含有指令，而這些指令告訴它要變成皮膚、骨頭還是血液。"},{"w":"nucleus","p":"n.","d":"the centre of a cell that holds the DNA","c":"細胞核","s":"We looked at onion cells under the microscope, and we could see a dark nucleus in the middle of each one.","t":"我們在顯微鏡下觀察洋蔥細胞，並能看見每個細胞中間都有一個深色的細胞核。"},{"w":"chromosome","p":"n.","d":"a thread-like structure in a cell that carries genes","c":"染色體","s":"Humans normally have 46 chromosome in each cell, and we receive half from our mother and half from our father.","t":"人類每個細胞通常有46條染色體，我們一半來自母親，一半來自父親。"},{"w":"gene","p":"n.","d":"a part of DNA that controls a feature like eye colour","c":"基因","s":"Scientists found a gene that affects how tall people grow, but food and sleep also play an important role.","t":"科學家發現了一個會影響人們長多高的基因，但食物和睡眠也扮演重要的角色。"},{"w":"double helix","p":"n.phr.","d":"the twisted ladder shape of DNA","c":"雙螺旋","s":"Our class built a model of DNA with sweets and sticks, and it twisted into a double helix just like the real thing.","t":"我們班用糖果和小棍子做了一個DNA模型，而它扭成了一個像真的一樣的雙螺旋。"},{"w":"base pair","p":"n.phr.","d":"two matching chemical units that form a step in DNA","c":"鹼基對","s":"Human DNA has about three billion base pair, so reading the whole code took scientists many years.","t":"人類DNA大約有三十億個鹼基對，所以科學家花了許多年才讀完整個密碼。"},{"w":"molecule","p":"n.","d":"the smallest unit of a substance made of atoms","c":"分子","s":"DNA is a very long molecule, but it is folded so tightly that it fits inside a tiny cell.","t":"DNA是一個非常長的分子，但它摺疊得非常緊密，所以能放進微小的細胞裡。"},{"w":"enzyme","p":"n.","d":"a substance in the body that speeds up chemical changes","c":"酵素","s":"Our saliva contains an enzyme that starts breaking down rice, so bread tastes sweeter if you chew it for a long time.","t":"我們的唾液含有一種會開始分解米飯的酵素，所以麵包嚼久了吃起來會比較甜。"},{"w":"cell division","p":"n.phr.","d":"the process in which one cell splits into two","c":"細胞分裂","s":"A cut on your finger heals quickly, because cell division makes new skin cells to fill the gap.","t":"你手指上的傷口很快就會癒合，因為細胞分裂會產生新的皮膚細胞來填補缺口。"},{"w":"membrane","p":"n.","d":"a thin layer that covers a cell","c":"薄膜","s":"The cell membrane works like a gate, and it decides which substances can enter or leave the cell.","t":"細胞薄膜就像一扇門，而它決定哪些物質可以進出細胞。"},{"w":"mitochondria","p":"n.","d":"parts of a cell that make energy","c":"粒線體","s":"Muscle cells contain many mitochondria, because they need a lot of energy when we run or lift things.","t":"肌肉細胞含有許多粒線體，因為我們跑步或舉東西時它們需要大量能量。"},{"w":"RNA","p":"n.","d":"a molecule that helps turn DNA instructions into proteins","c":"核糖核酸","s":"Some vaccines use RNA to teach the body how to fight a virus, and this new method was developed very quickly.","t":"有些疫苗利用核糖核酸教導身體如何對抗病毒，而這種新方法發展得非常快。"},{"w":"sequencing","p":"n.","d":"finding the exact order of units in DNA","c":"定序","s":"DNA sequencing used to cost millions of dollars, but now a person's whole genome can be read for a few hundred.","t":"DNA定序過去要花數百萬美元，但現在一個人的全基因組只要幾百美元就能讀取。"},{"w":"amino acid","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small unit that joins with others to build proteins","c":"胺基酸","s":"Meat, beans and eggs give us every amino acid we need, so vegetarians must choose their food carefully.","t":"肉類、豆類和蛋提供我們所需的每一種胺基酸，所以素食者必須小心選擇食物。"},{"w":"egg cell","p":"n.phr.","d":"the female cell that can grow into a baby","c":"卵細胞","s":"An egg cell is one of the largest cells in the human body, and you can almost see it without a microscope.","t":"卵細胞是人體中最大的細胞之一，而你幾乎不用顯微鏡就能看見它。"},{"w":"fertilisation","p":"n.","d":"when male and female cells join to start new life","c":"受精","s":"Frogs lay their eggs in the water of ponds, and fertilisation happens outside the mother's body there.","t":"青蛙把卵產在池塘的水中，而受精就在那裡、在母體之外發生。"},{"w":"embryo","p":"n.","d":"an animal or human in the very early stage of growth","c":"胚胎","s":"The chicken embryo grows inside the egg for about three weeks, and then the chick breaks the shell.","t":"雞的胚胎在蛋裡生長大約三週，然後小雞就會啄破蛋殼。"},{"w":"stem cell","p":"n.phr.","d":"a basic cell that can become many types of cell","c":"幹細胞","s":"Doctors hope that stem cell can repair damaged hearts, but more research is needed before this treatment is safe.","t":"醫生希望幹細胞能修復受損的心臟，但在這種治療安全之前還需要更多研究。"},{"w":"tissue","p":"n.","d":"a group of similar cells that work together","c":"組織","s":"The scientist took a small piece of tissue from the leaf, and she studied the cells under a microscope.","t":"科學家從葉子上取下一小片組織，並在顯微鏡下研究那些細胞。"},{"w":"organ","p":"n.","d":"a body part such as the heart that does a special job","c":"器官","s":"The skin is actually the largest organ of the human body, and it protects us from germs and heat.","t":"皮膚其實是人體最大的器官，而它保護我們免受細菌和高溫的傷害。"},{"w":"microbe","p":"n.","d":"a tiny living thing such as a bacterium","c":"微生物；細菌","s":"Yoghurt contains many friendly microbe, and they help our stomachs digest the food we eat more easily.","t":"優格含有許多有益的微生物，而它們幫助我們的胃更容易消化我們吃下的食物。"},{"w":"biochemistry","p":"n.","d":"the study of chemical processes in living things","c":"生物化學","s":"She enjoyed both biology and chemistry at school, so she decided to study biochemistry at university.","t":"她在學校時喜歡生物和化學兩科，所以她決定在大學主修生物化學。"},{"w":"geneticist","p":"n.","d":"a scientist who studies genes","c":"遺傳學家","s":"The geneticist explained the results to the family, and she said the baby's condition was not passed down from the parents.","t":"遺傳學家向這家人解釋了結果，並說寶寶的狀況並不是從父母遺傳下來的。"},{"w":"genetics","p":"n.","d":"the science of how features pass from parents to children","c":"遺傳學","s":"We studied genetics this term, and now I understand why I have curly hair like my grandfather.","t":"我們這學期學了遺傳學，現在我明白為什麼我會像祖父一樣有一頭捲髮。"},{"w":"petri dish","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small round dish used to grow germs in a lab","c":"培養皿","s":"We put a little bread in a petri dish, and after a week a green mould had covered it.","t":"我們在培養皿裡放了一點麵包，而一週後綠色的黴菌已經把它覆蓋了。"},{"w":"saliva","p":"n.","d":"the liquid in your mouth","c":"唾液","s":"The test only needs a little saliva, so you just spit into a small tube and send it to the lab.","t":"這項檢測只需要一點點唾液，所以你只要吐進一根小管子裡然後寄到實驗室。"},{"w":"cheek swab","p":"n.phr.","d":"a cotton stick rubbed inside the mouth to collect cells","c":"口腔拭子","s":"The police took a cheek swab from each worker, because they wanted to compare their DNA with the evidence.","t":"警方從每位員工身上採集了口腔拭子，因為他們想把他們的DNA和證據作比對。"},{"w":"decode","p":"v.","d":"to find the meaning of a code","c":"解碼；破譯","s":"Scientists worked for thirteen years to decode the human genome, and they finally finished the project in 2003.","t":"科學家努力了十三年來解碼人類基因組，並終於在2003年完成這項計畫。"},{"w":"twin","p":"n.","d":"one of two children born at the same time to the same mother","c":"雙胞胎","s":"My friend is a twin, and even our teachers cannot tell her and her sister apart.","t":"我的朋友是雙胞胎之一，連我們的老師都分不出她和她的姐妹。"},{"w":"cellular","p":"adj.","d":"relating to cells","c":"細胞的","s":"Smoking causes damage at a cellular level, so the harm starts long before a person notices any illness.","t":"吸菸會在細胞的層面造成傷害，所以傷害早在一個人察覺任何疾病之前就開始了。"},{"w":"fruit fly","p":"n.phr.","d":"a tiny fly often used in genetics experiments","c":"果蠅","s":"Scientists often study the fruit fly, because it breeds very quickly and shares many genes with humans.","t":"科學家常常研究果蠅，因為牠繁殖得非常快，而且和人類有許多共同的基因。"},{"w":"lab rat","p":"n.phr.","d":"a rat used for scientific experiments","c":"實驗鼠","s":"The new medicine was first tested on a lab rat, but it must also be tested on human volunteers before it is sold.","t":"這種新藥先在實驗鼠身上做了測試，但在販售之前也必須在人類志願者身上測試。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","cards":[{"w":"inheritance","p":"n.","d":"features passed from parents to children","c":"遺傳","s":"Curly hair in our family is a clear case of inheritance, because my mother, my grandmother and I all have it.","t":"我們家的捲髮是遺傳的明顯例子，因為我媽媽、我外婆和我都有捲髮。"},{"w":"mutation","p":"n.","d":"a change in a gene","c":"突變","s":"A small mutation in one gene gave the cat six toes on each paw, and her kittens had extra toes too.","t":"一個基因的小突變讓這隻貓每隻腳掌都有六根趾頭，而牠的小貓也有多出來的趾頭。"},{"w":"mutate","p":"v.","d":"to change in form because of a gene change","c":"突變","s":"Flu viruses mutate quickly every single year, so many people need a new vaccine each autumn.","t":"流感病毒每一年都快速突變，所以許多人每年秋天都需要接種新疫苗。"},{"w":"recessive","p":"adj.","d":"only shown when a child gets the same gene from both parents","c":"隱性的","s":"Blue eyes are caused by a recessive gene, so two brown-eyed parents can still have a blue-eyed baby.","t":"藍眼睛是由隱性的基因造成的，所以兩個棕眼睛的父母仍然可能生下藍眼睛的寶寶。"},{"w":"genotype","p":"n.","d":"the set of genes a living thing has","c":"基因型","s":"Two plants may look the same, but they can have a different genotype, so their seeds may grow differently.","t":"兩株植物可能看起來一樣，但它們可能有不同的基因型，所以它們的種子可能長得不一樣。"},{"w":"phenotype","p":"n.","d":"the features you can see, such as size or colour","c":"表現型","s":"A person's phenotype includes height and hair colour, and it depends on both genes and lifestyle.","t":"一個人的表現型包括身高和髮色，而它取決於基因和生活方式兩者。"},{"w":"carrier","p":"n.","d":"a person who has a gene but does not show its effect","c":"帶原者；攜帶者","s":"My uncle is a carrier of the gene, but he is healthy, so the doctor told him to tell his children.","t":"我舅舅是這個基因的攜帶者，但他很健康，所以醫生要他告訴他的孩子們。"},{"w":"gene pool","p":"n.phr.","d":"all the genes in a group of animals or people","c":"基因庫","s":"The small island population has a limited gene pool, so the zoo brought in new animals from other places.","t":"這個小島族群的基因庫很有限，所以動物園從其他地方引進了新的動物。"},{"w":"inbreeding","p":"n.","d":"breeding between closely related animals","c":"近親繁殖","s":"Many purebred dogs suffer from health problems, because years of inbreeding have made their genes too similar.","t":"許多純種狗受健康問題所苦，因為多年的近親繁殖讓牠們的基因太過相似。"},{"w":"eye colour","p":"n.phr.","d":"the colour of the coloured part of the eye","c":"眼睛顏色","s":"Most babies in Taiwan are born with dark eyes, but eye colour can change during the first year in some children.","t":"台灣大多數嬰兒出生時是深色眼睛，但有些孩子的眼睛顏色在第一年內可能會改變。"},{"w":"freckle","p":"n.","d":"a small brown spot on the skin","c":"雀斑","s":"She has many freckle on her nose like her father, and they get darker when she spends time in the sun.","t":"她的鼻子上有很多雀斑，跟她爸爸一樣，而且她曬太陽時雀斑會變得更深。"},{"w":"dimple","p":"n.","d":"a small hollow in the cheek when you smile","c":"酒窩","s":"Everyone in the family has a dimple in the left cheek, so people can easily guess that we are related.","t":"家裡每個人的左臉頰都有一個酒窩，所以人們很容易猜到我們是一家人。"},{"w":"left-handed","p":"adj.","d":"using the left hand more easily than the right","c":"左撇子的","s":"Both of my parents are left-handed, so it was not surprising that I also write with my left hand.","t":"我的父母都是左撇子的，所以我也用左手寫字並不令人意外。"},{"w":"birth defect","p":"n.phr.","d":"a health problem that a baby is born with","c":"先天缺陷","s":"Doctors advise pregnant women to take certain vitamins, because they lower the risk of a birth defect.","t":"醫生建議孕婦服用某些維生素，因為它們能降低先天缺陷的風險。"},{"w":"congenital","p":"adj.","d":"present from birth","c":"先天的","s":"The puppy had a congenital heart problem, but the vet performed an operation and it now runs around happily.","t":"那隻小狗有先天的心臟問題，但獸醫為牠動了手術，現在牠開心地到處跑。"},{"w":"blood type","p":"n.phr.","d":"the group your blood belongs to, such as A or O","c":"血型","s":"Your blood type is passed down from your parents, so a family's types can help doctors find a match.","t":"你的血型是從父母遺傳下來的，所以一個家庭的血型可以幫助醫生找到配對。"},{"w":"pedigree","p":"n.","d":"the recorded family history of an animal","c":"血統證明；系譜","s":"The breeder showed us the puppy's pedigree, and it listed the dog's parents and grandparents.","t":"繁殖者給我們看了小狗的血統證明，而上面列出了這隻狗的父母和祖父母。"},{"w":"purebred","p":"adj.","d":"having parents of the same breed","c":"純種的","s":"A purebred cat can be very expensive, but shelter cats are often healthier and cost much less.","t":"一隻純種的貓可能非常昂貴，但收容所的貓往往更健康，花費也少得多。"},{"w":"crossbreed","p":"v.","d":"to mix two breeds to make a new type","c":"雜交育種","s":"Farmers crossbred two kinds of rice, and the new type grows well in dry weather.","t":"農民把兩種稻米雜交育種，而新品種在乾燥的天氣中長得很好。"},{"w":"upbringing","p":"n.","d":"the way a child is cared for and taught at home","c":"教養；成長環境","s":"Twins who grow up apart can be very similar, but their upbringing still shapes their habits and interests.","t":"分開長大的雙胞胎可能非常相似，但他們的成長環境仍會塑造他們的習慣和興趣。"},{"w":"epigenetics","p":"n.","d":"the study of how lifestyle can switch genes on or off","c":"表觀遺傳學","s":"epigenetics shows that stress and diet can affect how our genes work, although the DNA itself does not change.","t":"表觀遺傳學顯示壓力和飲食會影響我們的基因如何運作，雖然DNA本身並沒有改變。"},{"w":"fraternal","p":"adj.","d":"(of twins) from two different eggs","c":"異卵的","s":"My brother and I are fraternal twins, so we look quite different and we were born ten minutes apart.","t":"我哥哥和我是異卵的雙胞胎，所以我們長得很不一樣，而且出生時間相差十分鐘。"},{"w":"sibling","p":"n.","d":"a brother or sister","c":"兄弟姊妹","s":"Each sibling in my family has a different hobby, although we all grew up in the same small apartment.","t":"我家的每個兄弟姊妹都有不同的嗜好，雖然我們都在同一間小公寓長大。"},{"w":"biological parent","p":"n.phr.","d":"the parent who gave you your genes","c":"親生父母","s":"Adopted children sometimes want to find their biological parent, because they are curious about their family history.","t":"被收養的孩子有時想找到他們的親生父母，因為他們對自己的家族史感到好奇。"},{"w":"gene expression","p":"n.phr.","d":"how strongly a gene is turned on in a cell","c":"基因表現","s":"Exercise can change gene expression in muscle cells, so regular training helps the body build stronger muscles.","t":"運動可以改變肌肉細胞中的基因表現，所以規律訓練能幫助身體練出更強壯的肌肉。"},{"w":"heritable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be passed from parent to child","c":"可遺傳的","s":"Height is highly heritable, but children today are taller than their grandparents because they eat better food.","t":"身高是高度可遺傳的，但今天的孩子比他們的祖父母高，因為他們吃得更好。"},{"w":"birthmark","p":"n.","d":"a coloured mark on the skin from birth","c":"胎記","s":"The baby has a small red birthmark on her arm, but the doctor said it will fade as she grows.","t":"寶寶的手臂上有一個小小的紅色胎記，但醫生說它會隨著她長大而變淡。"},{"w":"colour blindness","p":"n.phr.","d":"being unable to see some colours clearly","c":"色盲","s":"colour blindness is much more common in boys, because the gene for it is carried on the X chromosome.","t":"色盲在男孩中常見得多，因為與它相關的基因位於X染色體上。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","cards":[{"w":"CRISPR","p":"n.","d":"a tool that lets scientists cut and change DNA","c":"基因剪刀CRISPR","s":"Scientists used CRISPR to remove a disease gene from mice, and the treated mice stayed healthy.","t":"科學家使用基因剪刀CRISPR從老鼠身上移除一個致病基因，而接受治療的老鼠保持健康。"},{"w":"gene therapy","p":"n.phr.","d":"treating illness by changing a patient's genes","c":"基因療法","s":"The boy could not see well since birth, but gene therapy improved his sight, and now he can read books.","t":"這個男孩從出生起視力就不好，但基因療法改善了他的視力，現在他可以讀書了。"},{"w":"paternity test","p":"n.phr.","d":"a DNA test to find out who a child's father is","c":"親子鑑定","s":"The court asked for a paternity test, because the man said he was not the child's father.","t":"法院要求進行親子鑑定，因為那名男子說他不是孩子的父親。"},{"w":"forensic","p":"adj.","d":"using science to help solve crimes","c":"鑑識的","s":"The forensic team found a single hair at the scene, and its DNA led them to the thief.","t":"鑑識的小組在現場發現了一根頭髮，而它的DNA帶領他們找到了小偷。"},{"w":"transgenic","p":"adj.","d":"having genes added from another species","c":"基因轉殖的","s":"The lab created transgenic goats that produce a useful medicine in their milk, so patients can get it more cheaply.","t":"實驗室培育出基因轉殖的山羊，牠們的奶中含有一種有用的藥物，所以病人能更便宜地取得。"},{"w":"designer baby","p":"n.phr.","d":"a baby whose genes are chosen or changed by parents","c":"訂製嬰兒","s":"Many people worry about the idea of a designer baby, because rich parents might choose intelligence or good looks for their children.","t":"許多人擔心訂製嬰兒的想法，因為有錢的父母可能會為孩子挑選聰明才智或好看的外表。"},{"w":"bioethics","p":"n.","d":"the study of right and wrong in medicine and biology","c":"生命倫理學","s":"Our class debated gene editing in a bioethics lesson, and most students felt it should only be used to cure disease.","t":"我們班在一堂生命倫理學課上辯論基因編輯，而大多數學生認為它只應該被用來治療疾病。"},{"w":"precision medicine","p":"n.phr.","d":"treatment planned for a person's own genes","c":"精準醫療","s":"precision medicine lets doctors choose the right cancer drug for each patient, so the treatment works better and causes fewer problems.","t":"精準醫療讓醫生能為每位病人選擇合適的抗癌藥物，所以治療效果更好，產生的問題也更少。"},{"w":"insulin","p":"n.","d":"a hormone that controls sugar in the blood","c":"胰島素","s":"Today, bacteria are used to make human insulin, so it is much cheaper than it was fifty years ago.","t":"今天人們利用細菌來製造人類胰島素，所以它比五十年前便宜得多。"},{"w":"pharmaceutical","p":"adj.","d":"relating to making and selling medicines","c":"製藥的","s":"A large pharmaceutical company paid for the research, but the scientists promised to share their results with everyone.","t":"一家大型製藥的公司資助了這項研究，但科學家承諾會與所有人分享他們的研究結果。"},{"w":"clinical trial","p":"n.phr.","d":"a test of a new treatment on volunteers","c":"臨床試驗","s":"My aunt joined a clinical trial for a new medicine, and the nurses checked her health every week.","t":"我阿姨參加了一項新藥的臨床試驗，而護理師每週都檢查她的健康狀況。"},{"w":"test tube","p":"n.phr.","d":"a thin glass tube used in science labs","c":"試管","s":"The student carefully poured the blue liquid into a test tube, and then she added two drops of acid.","t":"那位學生小心地把藍色液體倒進試管，然後她加了兩滴酸液。"},{"w":"IVF","p":"n.","d":"a method of joining egg and sperm outside the body","c":"試管嬰兒療程","s":"The couple tried for years to have a baby, so they finally chose IVF, and their daughter was born last spring.","t":"這對夫妻多年來一直想要孩子，所以他們最後選擇了試管嬰兒療程，而他們的女兒在去年春天出生。"},{"w":"donor","p":"n.","d":"a person who gives blood or body parts to help others","c":"捐贈者","s":"My father is a blood donor, and he visits the blood centre every few months to help patients.","t":"我爸爸是一位捐血者，而他每隔幾個月就會去捐血中心幫助病人。"},{"w":"bone marrow","p":"n.phr.","d":"the soft tissue inside bones that makes blood","c":"骨髓","s":"The girl needed new bone marrow, and luckily a stranger with a matching type agreed to help her.","t":"那個女孩需要新的骨髓，幸運的是一位配型相符的陌生人同意幫助她。"},{"w":"biobank","p":"n.","d":"a store of blood and DNA samples for research","c":"生物資料庫","s":"Thousands of volunteers gave samples to the national biobank, so scientists can study which genes are linked to illness.","t":"數千名志願者把樣本提供給國家生物資料庫，好讓科學家研究哪些基因和疾病有關。"},{"w":"de-extinction","p":"n.","d":"bringing an extinct animal back to life","c":"復活滅絕物種","s":"Some companies are working on de-extinction, but critics say we should protect living animals first.","t":"有些公司正在研究復活滅絕物種，但批評者說我們應該先保護現存的動物。"},{"w":"gene drive","p":"n.phr.","d":"a method to spread a gene quickly through a population","c":"基因驅動","s":"Scientists hope a gene drive could stop mosquitoes from carrying malaria, but releasing them into the wild is risky.","t":"科學家希望基因驅動能阻止蚊子傳播瘧疾，但把牠們釋放到野外是有風險的。"},{"w":"pest-resistant","p":"adj.","d":"not easily damaged by insects","c":"抗蟲害的","s":"The farmer planted a pest-resistant type of corn, so he did not need to spray as many chemicals.","t":"那位農夫種了一種抗蟲害的玉米，所以他不需要噴灑那麼多化學藥劑。"},{"w":"golden rice","p":"n.phr.","d":"rice changed to contain more vitamin A","c":"黃金米","s":"golden rice was created to help poor children get vitamin A, but some groups still oppose it.","t":"黃金米是為了幫助貧窮兒童獲得維生素A而研發的，但有些團體仍然反對它。"},{"w":"fluorescent","p":"adj.","d":"giving off bright light under special lamps","c":"螢光的","s":"Scientists added a jellyfish gene to the fish, and now they look fluorescent green under blue light.","t":"科學家把一個水母基因加進魚的體內，而現在牠們在藍光下看起來是螢光的綠色。"},{"w":"glow-in-the-dark","p":"adj.","d":"shining in darkness","c":"夜光的","s":"My little brother loves his glow-in-the-dark stickers, and he puts them on his ceiling so he can see stars at night.","t":"我弟弟很喜歡他的夜光的貼紙，而他把它們貼在天花板上，這樣晚上就能看到星星。"},{"w":"treatment","p":"n.","d":"medical care for an illness or injury","c":"治療","s":"The new treatment is expensive, but the government will pay for it because it can save many lives.","t":"這種新治療很昂貴，但政府會支付費用，因為它能拯救許多生命。"},{"w":"spit","p":"v.","d":"to force liquid out of your mouth","c":"吐（口水）","s":"For the ancestry kit, I spat into a small tube, and a month later I got a report about my family's roots.","t":"為了做祖源檢測組，我吐口水到一根小管子裡，一個月後我收到了一份關於我家族根源的報告。"},{"w":"kit","p":"n.","d":"a set of things packed together for a task","c":"套組；工具包","s":"You can buy a DNA testing kit online, but experts say the health results are not always accurate.","t":"你可以在網路上買到DNA檢測套組，但專家說健康方面的結果不一定準確。"},{"w":"biomedical","p":"adj.","d":"relating to biology and medicine","c":"生物醫學的","s":"Taiwan has invested heavily in biomedical research, and many young scientists now work on new cancer treatments.","t":"台灣大量投資於生物醫學的研究，現在許多年輕科學家致力於新的癌症治療。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","cards":[{"w":"ethology","p":"n.","d":"the scientific study of animal behaviour","c":"動物行為學","s":"She became interested in ethology after watching birds in the park, and she now studies how crows solve puzzles.","t":"她在公園裡觀察鳥類之後對動物行為學產生了興趣，現在她研究烏鴉如何解決難題。"},{"w":"ethologist","p":"n.","d":"a scientist who studies animal behaviour","c":"動物行為學家","s":"The ethologist watched the wolves from a hidden hut, because she did not want her presence to change their behaviour.","t":"那位動物行為學家從一間隱蔽的小屋觀察狼群，因為她不希望自己的存在改變牠們的行為。"},{"w":"learned behaviour","p":"n.phr.","d":"an action an animal learns rather than is born with","c":"學習行為","s":"Opening milk bottles was a learned behaviour among some birds in Britain, and young birds copied it from older ones.","t":"在英國，打開牛奶瓶是某些鳥類的學習行為，而年輕的鳥從年長的鳥那裡模仿學會了。"},{"w":"imprinting","p":"n.","d":"a young animal's quick bond with the first thing it sees","c":"銘印","s":"Because of imprinting, the baby geese followed the scientist everywhere, and they treated him like their mother.","t":"由於銘印，小鵝到處跟著那位科學家，而且牠們把他當作媽媽。"},{"w":"conditioning","p":"n.","d":"training by linking an action with a reward or result","c":"制約","s":"My dog runs to the kitchen when she hears the fridge open, and this is a simple example of conditioning.","t":"我的狗一聽到冰箱打開就跑到廚房，而這是制約的一個簡單例子。"},{"w":"reflex","p":"n.","d":"an automatic movement you do not think about","c":"反射動作","s":"When the ball flew towards his face, he closed his eyes as a reflex, and he did not even think about it.","t":"當球朝他的臉飛來時，他閉上眼睛作為反射動作，而他甚至沒有思考。"},{"w":"birdsong","p":"n.","d":"the musical sounds that birds make","c":"鳥鳴","s":"I wake up to birdsong every morning in spring, because the birds sing loudly to attract partners.","t":"春天每天早上我都在鳥鳴聲中醒來，因為鳥兒大聲歌唱來吸引伴侶。"},{"w":"chirp","p":"v.","d":"(of a bird or insect) to make a short high sound","c":"啁啾；吱吱叫","s":"The baby birds chirp loudly whenever their mother returns, and the loudest one usually gets fed first.","t":"每當媽媽回來時，雛鳥就大聲吱吱叫，而叫得最大聲的那隻通常最先被餵食。"},{"w":"howl","p":"v.","d":"to make a long, loud crying sound","c":"嚎叫","s":"Wolves howl to call their pack together, and the sound can travel for many kilometres at night.","t":"狼嚎叫來召集狼群，而這種聲音在夜晚可以傳到好幾公里遠。"},{"w":"growl","p":"v.","d":"to make a low, angry sound in the throat","c":"低吼","s":"The dog began to growl when the stranger came near, so the man stepped back slowly.","t":"當陌生人靠近時，那隻狗開始低吼，所以那個人慢慢地往後退。"},{"w":"purr","p":"v.","d":"(of a cat) to make a soft, low sound when happy","c":"呼嚕叫","s":"My cat likes to purr on my lap in the evening, and the soft sound helps me relax after school.","t":"我的貓喜歡晚上在我腿上呼嚕叫，而那柔和的聲音幫助我放學後放鬆。"},{"w":"hiss","p":"v.","d":"to make a sound like a long \"sss\"","c":"發出嘶嘶聲","s":"The snake began to hiss when we came close, so we quickly moved away from the rocks.","t":"當我們靠近時那條蛇開始發出嘶嘶聲，所以我們迅速離開那些岩石。"},{"w":"echolocation","p":"n.","d":"finding objects by sending out sounds and hearing echoes","c":"回聲定位","s":"Bats use echolocation to catch insects in the dark, so they can hunt even when there is no moonlight.","t":"蝙蝠利用回聲定位在黑暗中捕捉昆蟲，所以即使沒有月光牠們也能狩獵。"},{"w":"pheromone","p":"n.","d":"a chemical an animal releases to send a message","c":"費洛蒙","s":"Ants leave a pheromone trail on the ground, and other ants follow it to find the food.","t":"螞蟻在地上留下費洛蒙的足跡，而其他螞蟻會跟著它找到食物。"},{"w":"scent","p":"n.","d":"a smell, especially one left by an animal","c":"氣味","s":"The tiger rubs its face on trees to leave its scent, and other tigers know to stay away.","t":"老虎用臉磨蹭樹木留下牠的氣味，而其他老虎就知道要遠離。"},{"w":"body language","p":"n.phr.","d":"messages sent by the way you move or stand","c":"肢體語言","s":"A dog's body language tells you a lot, because a low tail and flat ears often mean it is afraid.","t":"一隻狗的肢體語言能告訴你很多事，因為低垂的尾巴和平貼的耳朵通常表示牠很害怕。"},{"w":"alarm call","p":"n.phr.","d":"a sound an animal makes to warn others of danger","c":"警戒叫聲","s":"When a monkey sees an eagle, it gives a special alarm call, and the whole group hides in the trees.","t":"當一隻猴子看見老鷹時，牠會發出特別的警戒叫聲，而整個群體就躲進樹裡。"},{"w":"waggle dance","p":"n.phr.","d":"a dance bees do to show where food is","c":"搖擺舞","s":"A honeybee performs a waggle dance inside the hive, and the other bees learn the direction of the flowers.","t":"一隻蜜蜂在蜂巢內跳搖擺舞，而其他蜜蜂就知道花朵的方向。"},{"w":"whisker","p":"n.","d":"one of the long stiff hairs near an animal's mouth","c":"鬍鬚","s":"A cat uses each whisker to measure narrow spaces, so you should never cut them off.","t":"貓用每一根鬍鬚來測量狹窄的空間，所以你絕對不應該把它們剪掉。"},{"w":"antenna","p":"n.","d":"one of two long thin parts on an insect's head","c":"觸角","s":"The ant touched the other ant with its antenna, and in this way it could smell who belonged to its nest.","t":"那隻螞蟻用觸角碰觸另一隻螞蟻，而藉此牠能聞出誰屬於牠的蟻巢。"},{"w":"wag","p":"v.","d":"to move quickly from side to side","c":"搖動（尾巴）","s":"Dogs usually wag their tails when they are happy, but a stiff wagging tail can sometimes be a warning.","t":"狗開心時通常會搖動尾巴，但僵硬地搖尾巴有時可能是一種警告。"},{"w":"threat display","p":"n.phr.","d":"actions an animal uses to scare an enemy","c":"威嚇展示","s":"The cat arched its back and made its fur stand up in a threat display, so the bigger dog decided to leave.","t":"那隻貓拱起背、讓毛豎起來做出威嚇展示，所以那隻較大的狗決定離開。"},{"w":"warning colours","p":"n.phr.","d":"bright colours that tell enemies an animal is dangerous","c":"警戒色","s":"Poison dart frogs have bright warning colours, so birds learn quickly that these frogs are not safe to eat.","t":"箭毒蛙有鮮豔的警戒色，所以鳥類很快就學會這些青蛙吃了不安全。"},{"w":"play dead","p":"v.phr.","d":"to lie still and pretend to be dead","c":"裝死","s":"When a fox comes near, the opossum may play dead, and the fox often loses interest and walks away.","t":"當狐狸靠近時，負鼠可能會裝死，而狐狸常常失去興趣然後走開。"},{"w":"migratory","p":"adj.","d":"moving to another place each season","c":"遷徙的","s":"Taiwan is an important stop for many migratory birds, and birdwatchers gather at the coast every autumn.","t":"台灣是許多遷徙的鳥類的重要中途站，而賞鳥人士每年秋天都聚集在海岸邊。"},{"w":"homing","p":"adj.","d":"able to find the way home from far away","c":"歸巢的","s":"People once used homing pigeons to carry messages, because the birds always returned to their own nests.","t":"人們曾經利用歸巢的鴿子傳遞訊息，因為這些鳥總會回到自己的巢。"},{"w":"feral","p":"adj.","d":"once tame but now living wild","c":"野化的","s":"Many feral cats live near the old market, and volunteers feed them and take them to the vet.","t":"許多野化的貓住在舊市場附近，而志工們餵養牠們並帶牠們去看獸醫。"},{"w":"tool use","p":"n.phr.","d":"using objects to help get food or do tasks","c":"工具使用","s":"Sea otters break shells with stones, and this tool use shows that clever behaviour is not only found in apes.","t":"海獺用石頭敲開貝殼，而這種工具使用顯示聰明的行為不只出現在猿類身上。"},{"w":"mirror test","p":"n.phr.","d":"a test to see if an animal recognises itself in a mirror","c":"鏡子測驗","s":"Elephants and dolphins have passed the mirror test, so scientists believe they have some idea of who they are.","t":"大象和海豚都通過了鏡子測驗，所以科學家相信牠們對自己是誰有某種概念。"},{"w":"parrot","p":"n.","d":"a colourful bird that can copy human speech","c":"鸚鵡","s":"My neighbour's parrot can say twenty words, and it always says hello when someone opens the door.","t":"我鄰居的鸚鵡會說二十個字，而且每當有人開門時牠都會打招呼。"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","cards":[{"w":"pack","p":"n.","d":"a group of wolves or wild dogs","c":"（狼）群","s":"A wolf pack hunts together, so they can catch animals much larger than any single wolf.","t":"一群狼會一起狩獵，所以牠們能捕捉比任何一隻狼都大得多的動物。"},{"w":"troop","p":"n.","d":"a group of monkeys","c":"（猴）群","s":"A troop of monkeys stole the tourists' snacks, and the guide warned us to keep our bags closed.","t":"一群猴子偷走了遊客的零食，而導遊警告我們要把包包關好。"},{"w":"pod","p":"n.","d":"a group of whales or dolphins","c":"（鯨豚）群","s":"We saw a pod of dolphins from the boat, and they jumped beside us for almost ten minutes.","t":"我們從船上看到一群海豚，而牠們在我們旁邊跳躍了將近十分鐘。"},{"w":"swarm","p":"n.","d":"a large moving group of insects","c":"（昆蟲）一大群","s":"A swarm of bees landed on the school gate, so the teachers kept the students inside until it left.","t":"一大群蜜蜂停在學校大門上，所以老師們讓學生待在室內直到牠們離開。"},{"w":"hive","p":"n.","d":"a home where bees live together","c":"蜂巢","s":"Each hive has thousands of bees, but they all work together to collect food and protect the queen.","t":"每個蜂巢裡有數千隻蜜蜂，但牠們全都一起合作採集食物並保護蜂后。"},{"w":"queen bee","p":"n.phr.","d":"the only female bee in a hive that lays eggs","c":"蜂后","s":"The queen bee can lay over a thousand eggs a day, while the worker bees feed her and clean the hive.","t":"蜂后一天可以產下超過一千顆卵，而工蜂則餵養她並清潔蜂巢。"},{"w":"worker ant","p":"n.phr.","d":"an ant that collects food and builds the nest","c":"工蟻","s":"Each worker ant can carry objects much heavier than itself, so a small group can move a whole dead insect.","t":"每隻工蟻都能搬運比自己重得多的東西，所以一小群工蟻就能搬動一整隻死掉的昆蟲。"},{"w":"termite","p":"n.","d":"a small insect that eats wood and lives in large groups","c":"白蟻","s":"termite in Africa build huge mounds of soil, and the tunnels inside keep the air cool.","t":"非洲的白蟻會建造巨大的土丘，而裡面的通道讓空氣保持涼爽。"},{"w":"alpha male","p":"n.phr.","d":"the most powerful male in a group","c":"首領雄性","s":"The alpha male eats first after a hunt, but he must also protect the group from danger.","t":"首領雄性在狩獵後最先進食，但他也必須保護群體免受危險。"},{"w":"pecking order","p":"n.phr.","d":"the order of rank within a group","c":"啄序；等級次序","s":"The hens quickly formed a pecking order, and the strongest hen always got the best place at the food bowl.","t":"母雞們很快就形成了啄序，而最強壯的母雞總是在食盆旁佔到最好的位置。"},{"w":"grooming","p":"n.","d":"cleaning another animal's fur","c":"理毛","s":"Monkeys spend hours on grooming each day, and this helps them build friendships within the group.","t":"猴子每天花好幾個小時理毛，而這幫助牠們在群體內建立友誼。"},{"w":"kin selection","p":"n.phr.","d":"helping relatives so that shared genes survive","c":"親屬選擇","s":"A bee may die to protect its hive, and scientists explain this with kin selection, because the other bees are its sisters.","t":"一隻蜜蜂可能會為了保護蜂巢而死，而科學家用親屬選擇來解釋這點，因為其他蜜蜂是牠的姊妹。"},{"w":"cooperative","p":"adj.","d":"working together with others","c":"合作的","s":"Lions are cooperative hunters, so they often surround a zebra from different sides before they attack.","t":"獅子是合作的獵手，所以牠們常常在攻擊前從不同方向包圍一隻斑馬。"},{"w":"selfless","p":"adj.","d":"caring more about others than yourself","c":"無私的","s":"The mother bird made a selfless move when she pretended to be hurt, and the fox followed her away from the chicks.","t":"母鳥假裝受傷，做出了無私的舉動，而狐狸跟著她離開了雛鳥。"},{"w":"freeloader","p":"n.","d":"someone who takes help but gives nothing back","c":"搭便車者；白吃白喝者","s":"In a vampire bat group, a freeloader who never shares blood is soon ignored, so the bats rarely cheat.","t":"在吸血蝠群體中，從不分享血液的搭便車者很快就會被冷落，所以蝙蝠很少作弊。"},{"w":"courtship","p":"n.","d":"actions an animal uses to attract a partner","c":"求偶","s":"The bird's courtship includes singing and dancing, and the female watches carefully before she chooses.","t":"這種鳥的求偶包括唱歌和跳舞，而雌鳥在選擇之前會仔細觀察。"},{"w":"plumage","p":"n.","d":"a bird's feathers","c":"羽毛","s":"The male's bright plumage attracts females, but it also makes him easier for hawks to see.","t":"雄鳥鮮豔的羽毛能吸引雌鳥，但也讓牠更容易被老鷹發現。"},{"w":"peacock","p":"n.","d":"a male bird with a large, colourful tail","c":"雄孔雀","s":"The peacock spread his beautiful tail in the park, and a crowd of children gathered to take photos.","t":"那隻雄孔雀在公園裡展開牠美麗的尾巴，而一群孩子聚集過來拍照。"},{"w":"monogamous","p":"adj.","d":"having only one partner","c":"一夫一妻制的","s":"Swans are mostly monogamous, so a pair often stays together and raises chicks for many years.","t":"天鵝大多是一夫一妻制的，所以一對天鵝常常會在一起並養育雛鳥好多年。"},{"w":"pair bond","p":"n.phr.","d":"a strong long-term link between two partners","c":"配偶關係","s":"Penguins form a pair bond each season, and the parents call to each other to find their partner in the crowd.","t":"企鵝每個季節都會建立配偶關係，而父母會互相呼叫，以便在擁擠的群體中找到伴侶。"},{"w":"brood","p":"n.","d":"a group of young birds born at the same time","c":"一窩幼鳥","s":"The duck led her brood across the road, and the drivers stopped their cars to let them pass.","t":"那隻鴨子帶著她的一窩幼鳥過馬路，而駕駛們停下車讓牠們通過。"},{"w":"clutch","p":"n.","d":"a group of eggs laid at one time","c":"一窩蛋","s":"The turtle buried her clutch of eggs in the warm sand, and then she returned to the sea.","t":"那隻海龜把她的一窩蛋埋在溫暖的沙子裡，然後回到海裡。"},{"w":"chick","p":"n.","d":"a baby bird","c":"雛鳥；小雞","s":"The hungry chick opened its mouth very wide, and its father pushed a small fish inside.","t":"那隻飢餓的雛鳥把嘴張得很大，而牠的爸爸把一條小魚塞了進去。"},{"w":"parental care","p":"n.phr.","d":"the ways parents look after their young","c":"親代照顧","s":"Most fish give little parental care, but some male seahorses carry and protect the babies themselves.","t":"大多數魚類很少提供親代照顧，但有些雄海馬會親自攜帶和保護寶寶。"},{"w":"nurse","p":"v.","d":"to feed a baby with milk from its mother","c":"哺乳","s":"The mother cat nurse her kittens every few hours, so she rarely leaves the box during the first week.","t":"母貓每隔幾個小時就哺乳她的小貓，所以她在第一週很少離開箱子。"},{"w":"vampire bat","p":"n.phr.","d":"a bat that feeds on the blood of animals","c":"吸血蝙蝠","s":"A hungry vampire bat can die after two nights without food, so friends share their meals to keep each other alive.","t":"一隻飢餓的吸血蝙蝠兩晚沒有進食就可能死亡，所以朋友之間會分享食物讓彼此活下去。"},{"w":"meerkat","p":"n.","d":"a small African animal that stands on its back legs","c":"狐獴","s":"One meerkat stands on a rock to watch for eagles, while the others dig for insects in the sand.","t":"一隻狐獴站在岩石上留意老鷹，而其他狐獴在沙地裡挖昆蟲。"},{"w":"lookout","p":"n.","d":"an animal or person who watches for danger","c":"守望者；哨兵","s":"The goose that acts as a lookout keeps its head up, and it honks loudly if a dog comes near.","t":"擔任守望者的那隻鵝會抬著頭，而如果有狗靠近牠就會大聲鳴叫。"},{"w":"matriarch","p":"n.","d":"an old female who leads a family group","c":"女族長","s":"The elephant matriarch remembers where water can be found, so the group follows her during dry seasons.","t":"象群的女族長記得哪裡可以找到水，所以群體在乾季會跟隨她。"},{"w":"division of labour","p":"n.phr.","d":"splitting work so each member does a different job","c":"分工","s":"Ant colonies have a clear division of labour, because some ants find food while others care for the young.","t":"蟻群有明確的分工，因為有些螞蟻尋找食物，而其他螞蟻照顧幼蟲。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 1 (analysis – initial)","cards":[{"w":"analysis","p":"n.","d":"a careful study of something to understand it","c":"分析","s":"The lab's analysis of the bones showed that the animal was young, so it probably died before it could have babies.","t":"實驗室對骨頭的分析顯示這隻動物很年輕，所以牠很可能在生育之前就死了。"},{"w":"prediction","p":"n.","d":"a statement about what will happen","c":"預測","s":"Darwin made a prediction about a moth with a very long tongue, and scientists finally found it forty years later.","t":"達爾文對一種舌頭極長的蛾做出了預測，而科學家終於在四十年後找到了牠。"},{"w":"approximation","p":"n.","d":"a number or idea that is close but not exact","c":"近似值；概算","s":"Six million years is only an approximation, because scientists cannot know exactly when humans and chimps split.","t":"六百萬年只是一個近似值，因為科學家無法確切知道人類和黑猩猩是何時分開的。"},{"w":"concentrate","p":"v.","d":"to give all your attention to something","c":"專注","s":"The cat seemed to concentrate completely on the mouse hole, and it did not move for almost an hour.","t":"那隻貓似乎完全專注在老鼠洞上，而且牠幾乎一個小時都沒有動。"},{"w":"essence","p":"n.","d":"the most important basic quality of something","c":"本質；精髓","s":"The essence of Darwin's idea is simple, but it took him more than twenty years to publish it.","t":"達爾文想法的本質很簡單，但他花了二十多年才把它發表出來。"},{"w":"activate","p":"v.","d":"to make something start working","c":"啟動；活化","s":"Sunlight can activate certain genes in your skin, so your skin becomes darker after a summer holiday.","t":"陽光能活化你皮膚中的某些基因，所以暑假過後你的皮膚會變得比較黑。"},{"w":"capture","p":"v.","d":"to catch an animal or person","c":"捕捉","s":"The team used soft nets to capture the birds, and they released them after putting small rings on their legs.","t":"研究團隊用柔軟的網子捕捉鳥類，並在牠們腳上套上小環後把牠們放走。"},{"w":"circumstantial","p":"adj.","d":"suggesting something but not proving it directly","c":"間接的；旁證的","s":"The evidence against the dog was only circumstantial, because nobody actually saw it eat the cake.","t":"對那隻狗不利的證據只是間接的，因為沒有人真的看見牠吃了蛋糕。"},{"w":"conditional","p":"adj.","d":"depending on something else happening","c":"有條件的","s":"The monkey's help was conditional, so it only shared food with monkeys that had shared with it before.","t":"那隻猴子的幫忙是有條件的，所以牠只和以前跟牠分享過食物的猴子分享。"},{"w":"contextual","p":"adj.","d":"depending on the situation around something","c":"情境的；與上下文有關的","s":"Students used contextual clues to guess the meaning of \"gene pool\", and most of them guessed correctly.","t":"學生利用上下文的線索猜出「基因庫」的意思，而大多數人都猜對了。"},{"w":"debunk","p":"v.","d":"to show that a popular belief is false","c":"揭穿；駁斥","s":"Our teacher wanted to debunk the myth that goldfish only remember things for three seconds, so she showed us a study.","t":"我們老師想要駁斥金魚只有三秒記憶的迷思，所以她給我們看了一項研究。"},{"w":"exterminate","p":"v.","d":"to kill all of a group of animals","c":"撲滅；滅絕","s":"The city decided to exterminate the rats near the market, but some people asked for a kinder solution.","t":"市政府決定撲滅市場附近的老鼠，但有些人要求更溫和的解決辦法。"},{"w":"foreshadow","p":"v.","d":"to show signs of something that will happen later","c":"預示","s":"Small changes in the birds' songs may foreshadow the birth of a new species, although it could take thousands of years.","t":"鳥鳴中的小變化可能預示一個新物種的誕生，雖然這可能需要數千年。"},{"w":"implicate","p":"v.","d":"to show that something is involved in a problem","c":"牽涉；顯示與…有關","s":"The study seemed to implicate one gene in the disease, but the scientists said more tests were needed.","t":"這項研究似乎顯示一個基因與這種疾病有關，但科學家說還需要更多測試。"},{"w":"interfere","p":"v.","d":"to get involved and cause problems","c":"干擾","s":"Tourists should not interfere with nesting turtles, because bright lights and noise can scare them back into the sea.","t":"遊客不應該干擾正在築巢的海龜，因為強光和噪音會把牠們嚇回海裡。"},{"w":"intertwine","p":"v.","d":"to twist or link closely together","c":"交織；緊密相連","s":"Genes and environment intertwine in complex ways, so it is hard to say which one matters more.","t":"基因和環境以複雜的方式交織在一起，所以很難說哪一個更重要。"},{"w":"invalidate","p":"v.","d":"to show that something is not correct","c":"使無效；推翻","s":"One mistake in the data could invalidate the whole study, so the scientists checked every number twice.","t":"資料中的一個錯誤就可能推翻整個研究，所以科學家把每個數字都檢查了兩次。"},{"w":"moderate","p":"adj.","d":"not too much and not too little","c":"適度的；中等的","s":"The plants grew best at moderate temperatures, but they died quickly when the greenhouse became too hot.","t":"這些植物在適度的溫度下長得最好，但當溫室變得太熱時它們很快就死了。"},{"w":"neutralise","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from having an effect","c":"中和；使失效","s":"Some animals such as the mongoose can neutralise snake poison, so they can eat snakes without getting sick.","t":"有些像獴這樣的動物能中和蛇毒，所以牠們可以吃蛇而不會生病。"},{"w":"reaffirm","p":"v.","d":"to say again that something is true","c":"重申；再次確認","s":"The new fossils reaffirm the idea that birds came from dinosaurs, and few scientists now doubt it.","t":"新的化石再次確認了鳥類來自恐龍的觀點，而現在很少有科學家懷疑這一點。"},{"w":"sever","p":"v.","d":"to cut or break completely","c":"切斷","s":"The new highway may sever the path that the frogs use every spring, so the city built small tunnels under the road.","t":"新的高速公路可能會切斷青蛙每年春天使用的路徑，所以市政府在路下方建造了小隧道。"},{"w":"shed","p":"v.","d":"to lose skin, hair or leaves naturally","c":"脫落；蛻（皮）","s":"Snakes shed their skin several times a year, and you can sometimes find the old skin in the grass.","t":"蛇每年會蛻皮好幾次，而你有時可以在草叢裡找到舊的蛇皮。"},{"w":"stabilise","p":"v.","d":"to become steady and stop changing","c":"穩定下來","s":"The number of deer began to stabilise after wolves returned, and the forest plants slowly grew back.","t":"狼回來之後鹿的數量開始穩定下來，而森林裡的植物也慢慢長了回來。"},{"w":"symbolise","p":"v.","d":"to be a sign of an idea","c":"象徵","s":"In many cultures, the owl is used to symbolise wisdom, although owls are not cleverer than many other birds.","t":"在許多文化中，貓頭鷹被用來象徵智慧，雖然貓頭鷹並沒有比許多其他鳥類更聰明。"},{"w":"initial","p":"adj.","d":"happening at the beginning","c":"最初的","s":"The initial results looked exciting, but later tests showed that the gene had only a small effect.","t":"最初的結果看起來令人興奮，但後來的測試顯示這個基因只有很小的影響。"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 2 (anatomy – faulty)","cards":[{"w":"anatomy","p":"n.","d":"the structure of a body","c":"解剖構造；解剖學","s":"A bat's wing and a human hand have a similar anatomy, because both contain the same kinds of bones.","t":"蝙蝠的翅膀和人類的手有相似的解剖構造，因為兩者都包含相同種類的骨頭。"},{"w":"archetype","p":"n.","d":"a perfect typical example of something","c":"典型；原型","s":"The lion is the archetype of a powerful hunter in stories, but in real life the females do most of the hunting.","t":"獅子在故事中是強大獵手的典型，但在現實生活中大部分的狩獵是母獅做的。"},{"w":"bearing","p":"n.","d":"influence or connection","c":"關係；影響","s":"Your diet as a child may have a bearing on your health as an adult, so parents should offer healthy meals.","t":"你小時候的飲食可能對你成年後的健康有影響，所以父母應該提供健康的餐點。"},{"w":"chaos","p":"n.","d":"a state of complete confusion","c":"混亂","s":"The fox ran into the chicken house, and there was chaos as the birds flew in every direction.","t":"狐狸衝進雞舍，而雞群向四面八方飛竄，一片混亂。"},{"w":"collaboration","p":"n.","d":"working together with others","c":"合作","s":"The project was a collaboration between scientists from twenty countries, and they shared all their data online.","t":"這個計畫是來自二十個國家科學家之間的合作，而他們在網路上分享所有的資料。"},{"w":"conclusion","p":"n.","d":"a decision you reach after thinking","c":"結論","s":"After watching the crows for months, she came to the conclusion that they could recognise human faces.","t":"觀察烏鴉好幾個月之後，她得出了牠們能認出人臉的結論。"},{"w":"derivative","p":"n.","d":"something developed from something else","c":"衍生物","s":"Aspirin is a derivative of a chemical found in tree bark, and people used the bark as medicine long ago.","t":"阿斯匹靈是樹皮中一種化學物質的衍生物，而人們很久以前就把樹皮當作藥使用。"},{"w":"exception","p":"n.","d":"something that does not follow the usual rule","c":"例外","s":"Most mammals do not lay eggs, but the platypus is an exception, and that surprised early scientists.","t":"大多數哺乳類動物不會下蛋，但鴨嘴獸是例外，而這讓早期的科學家很驚訝。"},{"w":"fidelity","p":"n.","d":"loyalty to a partner","c":"忠誠","s":"Scientists once praised the fidelity of swans, but DNA tests showed that some chicks have a different father.","t":"科學家曾經讚揚天鵝的忠誠，但DNA檢測顯示有些雛鳥的父親是另一隻。"},{"w":"flaw","p":"n.","d":"a mistake or weakness","c":"缺陷；瑕疵","s":"There was a flaw in the experiment, because the scientists forgot to give one group of mice the same food.","t":"這個實驗有一個缺陷，因為科學家忘了給其中一組老鼠吃同樣的食物。"},{"w":"hindrance","p":"n.","d":"something that makes progress difficult","c":"阻礙","s":"A heavy tail can be a hindrance when a bird escapes from a predator, but it helps the bird attract a mate.","t":"沉重的尾巴在鳥逃離掠食者時可能是一種阻礙，但它能幫助鳥吸引配偶。"},{"w":"inclusion","p":"n.","d":"adding someone or something to a group","c":"納入；包含","s":"The inclusion of more women in the study was important, because earlier results were based mostly on men.","t":"在研究中納入更多女性很重要，因為先前的結果主要是基於男性。"},{"w":"inquiry","p":"n.","d":"an official question or investigation","c":"調查；詢問","s":"The university started an inquiry into the lab, because some results seemed too perfect to be true.","t":"大學對這間實驗室展開了調查，因為有些結果看起來完美得令人難以置信。"},{"w":"manifestation","p":"n.","d":"a sign that shows something exists","c":"表現；顯現","s":"Tail wagging is one manifestation of a dog's mood, but you should also watch its ears and eyes.","t":"搖尾巴是狗的情緒的一種表現，但你也應該觀察牠的耳朵和眼睛。"},{"w":"narrative","p":"n.","d":"a story or explanation of events","c":"敘事；說法","s":"The old narrative said humans left Africa only once, but new DNA evidence tells a more complex story.","t":"舊的說法認為人類只離開非洲一次，但新的DNA證據講述了一個更複雜的故事。"},{"w":"rebuttal","p":"n.","d":"an answer that shows something is wrong","c":"反駁","s":"The young scientist wrote a rebuttal to the article, and she used her own data to show its mistakes.","t":"那位年輕的科學家針對這篇文章寫了一篇反駁，而她用自己的資料指出文章的錯誤。"},{"w":"repertoire","p":"n.","d":"all the things a person or animal can do","c":"全部本領；曲目","s":"A mockingbird has a huge repertoire of songs, and it can even copy car alarms and phones.","t":"一隻嘲鶇擁有大量的曲目，而牠甚至能模仿汽車警報器和電話的聲音。"},{"w":"scepticism","p":"n.","d":"doubt about whether something is true","c":"懷疑態度","s":"Many people met the idea of talking dolphins with scepticism, because the early studies were very small.","t":"許多人以懷疑態度看待會說話的海豚這種想法，因為早期的研究規模很小。"},{"w":"subset","p":"n.","d":"a smaller group within a larger group","c":"子集；一部分","s":"Only a small subset of the birds learned the new song, but those birds attracted more females.","t":"只有一小部分的鳥學會了新的歌曲，但那些鳥吸引了更多雌鳥。"},{"w":"terminology","p":"n.","d":"special words used in a subject","c":"術語","s":"Genetics has a lot of difficult terminology, so our teacher gave us a word list before the lesson.","t":"遺傳學有很多困難的術語，所以我們老師在上課前給了我們一張單字表。"},{"w":"tolerance","p":"n.","d":"the ability to accept or survive something","c":"耐受力；容忍","s":"Some adults have no tolerance for milk, because their bodies stop making the enzyme after childhood.","t":"有些成年人對牛奶沒有耐受力，因為他們的身體在童年後就不再製造那種酵素。"},{"w":"accidental","p":"adj.","d":"happening by chance","c":"意外的","s":"The discovery was accidental, because the scientist was studying something else when she noticed the glowing cells.","t":"這個發現是意外的，因為那位科學家注意到發光細胞時正在研究別的東西。"},{"w":"asymmetrical","p":"adj.","d":"having two sides that are not the same","c":"不對稱的","s":"Some owls have asymmetrical ears, so they can tell exactly where a sound comes from in the dark.","t":"有些貓頭鷹的耳朵是不對稱的，所以牠們能在黑暗中精確分辨聲音從哪裡傳來。"},{"w":"deficient","p":"adj.","d":"not having enough of something","c":"缺乏的","s":"The puppies were deficient in vitamins, so the vet changed their food and they soon became stronger.","t":"那些小狗缺乏維生素，所以獸醫換了牠們的食物，而牠們很快就變得更強壯。"},{"w":"faulty","p":"adj.","d":"not working correctly","c":"有缺陷的；故障的","s":"A faulty gene can cause a serious illness, but sometimes doctors can treat it with new medicines.","t":"一個有缺陷的基因可能導致嚴重的疾病，但有時醫生可以用新藥治療。"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 3 (functional – mutually)","cards":[{"w":"functional","p":"adj.","d":"working and useful","c":"有功能的","s":"Ostriches have wings, but they are not functional for flying, so the birds use them for balance instead.","t":"鴕鳥有翅膀，但它們不是有功能的飛行翅膀，所以鴕鳥改用翅膀來保持平衡。"},{"w":"genuine","p":"adj.","d":"real and true","c":"真正的","s":"The dog showed genuine fear during the storm, so we let it sleep inside the house with us.","t":"那隻狗在暴風雨中表現出真正的恐懼，所以我們讓牠和我們一起睡在屋子裡。"},{"w":"identifiable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be recognised","c":"可辨認的","s":"Each zebra is identifiable by its stripes, because no two zebras have exactly the same pattern.","t":"每隻斑馬都可以藉由牠的條紋辨認出來，因為沒有兩隻斑馬的花紋完全相同。"},{"w":"illogical","p":"adj.","d":"not sensible or reasonable","c":"不合邏輯的","s":"It seems illogical for a bird to carry such a heavy tail, but the tail helps it win a partner.","t":"一隻鳥背負這麼沉重的尾巴似乎不合邏輯，但這條尾巴幫助牠贏得伴侶。"},{"w":"immune","p":"adj.","d":"not able to be affected by a disease","c":"免疫的","s":"Some people are immune to the virus, because they carry a rare gene that blocks it.","t":"有些人對這種病毒是免疫的，因為他們帶有一個能阻擋病毒的罕見基因。"},{"w":"independent","p":"adj.","d":"not needing help from others","c":"獨立的","s":"Young sea turtles are independent from the moment they hatch, so they must reach the sea without help.","t":"小海龜從孵化的那一刻起就是獨立的，所以牠們必須在沒有幫助的情況下抵達大海。"},{"w":"influential","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong effect on others","c":"有影響力的","s":"Darwin's book was very influential, and it changed the way people thought about nature and themselves.","t":"達爾文的書非常有影響力，而它改變了人們對大自然和自身的看法。"},{"w":"irrelevant","p":"adj.","d":"not connected to the subject","c":"無關的","s":"The colour of a dog's fur is irrelevant to its intelligence, so you cannot judge a dog by its coat.","t":"狗的毛色與牠的聰明程度無關，所以你不能以毛色來評斷一隻狗。"},{"w":"partial","p":"adj.","d":"not complete","c":"部分的","s":"The scientists found only a partial skeleton, but it was enough to show that the animal walked on two legs.","t":"科學家只找到了一副部分的骨骼，但這足以顯示這隻動物用兩條腿走路。"},{"w":"persistent","p":"adj.","d":"continuing for a long time","c":"持續的；堅持不懈的","s":"The persistent crow tried again and again to open the box, and finally it worked out how to lift the lid.","t":"那隻堅持不懈的烏鴉一次又一次地嘗試打開箱子，最後牠想出了如何掀開蓋子。"},{"w":"restrictive","p":"adj.","d":"limiting what people can do","c":"限制性的","s":"Some countries have very restrictive laws on gene editing, but others allow scientists to do much more research.","t":"有些國家對基因編輯有非常限制性的法律，但其他國家允許科學家進行更多研究。"},{"w":"static","p":"adj.","d":"not moving or changing","c":"靜止的；不變的","s":"People once thought species were static, but Darwin showed that they change slowly over time.","t":"人們曾經認為物種是不變的，但達爾文證明了它們會隨著時間慢慢改變。"},{"w":"unbiased","p":"adj.","d":"fair and not influenced by personal opinions","c":"不偏不倚的","s":"Scientists try to be unbiased when they watch animals, but it is easy to see human feelings where there are none.","t":"科學家觀察動物時盡量保持不偏不倚，但很容易在沒有人類情感的地方看到人類情感。"},{"w":"unreliable","p":"adj.","d":"not able to be trusted","c":"不可靠的","s":"Some cheap DNA tests are unreliable, so you should not make health decisions based on them alone.","t":"有些便宜的DNA檢測是不可靠的，所以你不應該只根據它們做健康方面的決定。"},{"w":"subsequently","p":"adv.","d":"after something else happened","c":"隨後","s":"The lab first tested the drug on mice, and they subsequently tested it on a small group of volunteers.","t":"實驗室先在老鼠身上測試這種藥物，而他們隨後又在一小群志願者身上進行測試。"},{"w":"widely","p":"adv.","d":"by many people or in many places","c":"廣泛地","s":"Darwin's theory is now widely accepted, but it caused angry arguments when it was first published.","t":"達爾文的理論現在被廣泛地接受，但它首次發表時曾引起激烈的爭論。"},{"w":"inherently","p":"adv.","d":"as a basic, natural part of something","c":"本質上；天生地","s":"Wolves are not inherently dangerous to people, but they may attack when they are very hungry or afraid.","t":"狼本質上對人類並不危險，但牠們在非常飢餓或害怕時可能會攻擊。"},{"w":"progressively","p":"adv.","d":"gradually, step by step","c":"逐步地","s":"The fish's fins became progressively stronger over millions of years, and finally they could support its body on land.","t":"經過數百萬年，這種魚的鰭逐步地變得更強壯，最後它們能在陸地上支撐牠的身體。"},{"w":"intentionally","p":"adv.","d":"on purpose","c":"故意地","s":"The bird intentionally dropped the nut onto the road, and it waited for a car to crack the shell.","t":"那隻鳥故意地把堅果丟到馬路上，然後等待汽車把殼壓碎。"},{"w":"collectively","p":"adv.","d":"as a group","c":"集體地","s":"The fish move collectively in a large school, so a shark finds it hard to focus on just one.","t":"魚群以大群集體地移動，所以鯊魚很難只專注在其中一條魚上。"},{"w":"partly","p":"adv.","d":"to some degree, but not completely","c":"部分地","s":"Your height is partly decided by your genes, but good food and enough sleep also help you grow.","t":"你的身高部分由基因決定，但良好的食物和充足的睡眠也能幫助你長高。"},{"w":"typically","p":"adv.","d":"usually","c":"通常","s":"Female cats typically have four to six kittens, and the mother looks after them for about two months.","t":"母貓通常會生四到六隻小貓，而貓媽媽會照顧牠們大約兩個月。"},{"w":"frequently","p":"adv.","d":"often","c":"經常","s":"Dolphins frequently help each other when one is hurt, and they lift the injured dolphin to the surface to breathe.","t":"當一隻海豚受傷時，海豚們經常互相幫助，而且牠們會把受傷的海豚托到水面呼吸。"},{"w":"therefore","p":"adv.","d":"for that reason","c":"因此","s":"The two birds cannot produce young together, and therefore scientists classify them as separate species.","t":"這兩種鳥無法一起生下後代，因此科學家把牠們歸類為不同的物種。"},{"w":"mutually","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that helps or affects both sides","c":"互相地","s":"The small fish clean the shark's teeth and get a free meal, so the relationship is mutually helpful.","t":"小魚清潔鯊魚的牙齒並得到一頓免費的餐點，所以這種關係是互相有益的。"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 4 (statistically – recognise)","cards":[{"w":"statistically","p":"adv.","d":"according to numbers and data","c":"統計上","s":"The difference between the two groups was not statistically important, so the scientists could not support their idea.","t":"兩組之間的差異在統計上並不顯著，所以科學家無法支持他們的想法。"},{"w":"uniquely","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that no other thing has","c":"獨特地","s":"Humans are uniquely good at learning languages, but many animals also communicate in surprising ways.","t":"人類在學習語言方面獨特地擅長，但許多動物也以令人驚訝的方式溝通。"},{"w":"sharply","p":"adv.","d":"suddenly and by a large amount","c":"急劇地","s":"The number of bees fell sharply last year, and farmers worried about their fruit trees.","t":"蜜蜂的數量去年急劇地下降，而農民們擔心他們的果樹。"},{"w":"drastically","p":"adv.","d":"in a sudden and extreme way","c":"大幅地；劇烈地","s":"The cost of reading DNA has fallen drastically, so many hospitals can now test patients' genes.","t":"讀取DNA的成本已經大幅地下降，所以現在許多醫院都能檢測病人的基因。"},{"w":"conceptualise","p":"v.","d":"to form an idea of something in your mind","c":"構想；概念化","s":"It is hard to conceptualise how long four billion years is, so our teacher compared Earth's history to a single day.","t":"很難構想四十億年有多長，所以我們老師把地球的歷史比喻成一天。"},{"w":"construe","p":"v.","d":"to understand something in a certain way","c":"理解；解讀","s":"People often construe a chimp's wide smile as happiness, but it usually means the animal is afraid.","t":"人們常常把黑猩猩咧嘴的笑容解讀為快樂，但那通常表示這隻動物很害怕。"},{"w":"deceive","p":"v.","d":"to make someone believe something false","c":"欺騙","s":"Some birds deceive their enemies by pretending to have a broken wing, and they lead the danger away from the nest.","t":"有些鳥會假裝翅膀受傷來欺騙牠們的敵人，並把危險引離巢穴。"},{"w":"differ","p":"v.","d":"to be not the same","c":"不同","s":"Human DNA does not differ much from person to person, so we are all more alike than we think.","t":"人類的DNA在人與人之間並沒有太大的不同，所以我們彼此比自己想像的更相似。"},{"w":"disprove","p":"v.","d":"to show that something is not true","c":"證明…是錯的","s":"The experiment was designed to disprove the old belief, and the results clearly showed that it was wrong.","t":"這個實驗是為了證明那個舊觀念是錯的而設計的，而結果清楚地顯示它確實錯了。"},{"w":"duplicate","p":"v.","d":"to make an exact copy","c":"複製","s":"Before a cell divides, it must duplicate its DNA, so each new cell gets a full set of instructions.","t":"細胞在分裂之前必須複製它的DNA，這樣每個新細胞才能得到一整套指令。"},{"w":"elapse","p":"v.","d":"(of time) to pass","c":"（時間）流逝","s":"Millions of years must elapse before a new species forms, so we rarely see it happen in our lifetime.","t":"必須流逝數百萬年才會形成一個新物種，所以我們很少在一生中看到它發生。"},{"w":"enrich","p":"v.","d":"to improve the quality of something","c":"豐富；充實","s":"Zoos enrich the lives of their animals with toys and puzzles, because bored animals can become stressed.","t":"動物園用玩具和益智遊戲來豐富動物的生活，因為無聊的動物會變得有壓力。"},{"w":"favour","p":"v.","d":"to give an advantage to","c":"有利於；偏好","s":"Cold weather tends to favour animals with thick fur, so mammals in the far north are usually furry.","t":"寒冷的天氣往往有利於毛皮厚的動物，所以極北地區的哺乳類通常都毛茸茸的。"},{"w":"infest","p":"v.","d":"(of insects or animals) to fill a place in large numbers","c":"大批出沒；侵擾","s":"Fleas can infest a house very quickly, so pet owners should check their animals regularly.","t":"跳蚤能很快地侵擾一間房子，所以寵物主人應該定期檢查他們的動物。"},{"w":"possess","p":"v.","d":"to have or own","c":"擁有","s":"Many birds possess a kind of compass in their eyes, and this helps them find their way across oceans.","t":"許多鳥類眼中擁有一種指南針，而這幫助牠們找到橫越海洋的路。"},{"w":"secrete","p":"v.","d":"to produce a liquid inside the body","c":"分泌","s":"Frogs secrete a slimy liquid from their skin, and it keeps them wet and protects them from germs.","t":"青蛙從皮膚分泌一種黏滑的液體，而它能保持牠們濕潤並保護牠們免受細菌感染。"},{"w":"alternate","p":"v.","d":"to take turns or change between two things","c":"輪流；交替","s":"The two parent birds alternate between sitting on the eggs and looking for food, so the eggs are never left cold.","t":"兩隻親鳥輪流孵蛋和尋找食物，所以蛋從來不會被留著變冷。"},{"w":"arouse","p":"v.","d":"to cause a feeling or reaction","c":"引起；激起","s":"The strange noise arouse the dog's curiosity, so it walked slowly towards the bushes to find out more.","t":"那奇怪的聲音激起了狗的好奇心，所以牠慢慢走向灌木叢想一探究竟。"},{"w":"attach","p":"v.","d":"to fix or join one thing to another","c":"附著；貼上","s":"Scientists attach tiny trackers to the turtles' shells, and they can follow the animals across the ocean.","t":"科學家把小型追蹤器貼在海龜殼上，而他們就能追蹤這些動物橫越海洋。"},{"w":"attract","p":"v.","d":"to make something come closer","c":"吸引","s":"Male frogs sing loudly to attract females, but the noise can also bring hungry bats.","t":"雄蛙大聲鳴叫以吸引雌蛙，但這噪音也可能招來飢餓的蝙蝠。"},{"w":"compete","p":"v.","d":"to try to win against others","c":"競爭","s":"Young male deer compete for the attention of females, and the winners are usually the largest ones.","t":"年輕的雄鹿為了吸引雌鹿的注意而競爭，而勝利者通常是體型最大的。"},{"w":"determine","p":"v.","d":"to decide or find out exactly","c":"決定；確定","s":"In some turtles, the sand temperature can determine whether a baby is male or female.","t":"在某些海龜中，沙子的溫度能決定寶寶是雄性還是雌性。"},{"w":"distract","p":"v.","d":"to take someone's attention away","c":"使分心","s":"The mother bird flies around noisily to distract the cat, while her chicks hide quietly in the nest.","t":"母鳥吵鬧地四處飛來使那隻貓分心，而她的雛鳥安靜地躲在巢裡。"},{"w":"foresee","p":"v.","d":"to know that something will happen","c":"預見","s":"Few scientists could foresee how quickly gene editing would develop, and now laws are struggling to keep up.","t":"很少有科學家能預見基因編輯會發展得這麼快，而現在法律正努力追趕。"},{"w":"recognise","p":"v.","d":"to know someone or something you have seen before","c":"認出","s":"Sheep can recognise the faces of other sheep, and they can remember them for up to two years.","t":"羊能認出其他羊的臉，而且牠們能記住長達兩年。"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 5 (regard – experimentation)","cards":[{"w":"regard","p":"v.","d":"to think of in a particular way","c":"視為；認為","s":"Many farmers regard crows as pests, but scientists see them as some of the cleverest birds on Earth.","t":"許多農民把烏鴉視為害鳥，但科學家把牠們看作地球上最聰明的鳥類之一。"},{"w":"relate","p":"v.","d":"to find or show a connection","c":"有關聯；與…相關","s":"Scientists are trying to relate certain genes to sleep habits, because some people need much less sleep than others.","t":"科學家正試著把某些基因與睡眠習慣相關聯，因為有些人需要的睡眠比別人少得多。"},{"w":"simplify","p":"v.","d":"to make something easier to understand","c":"簡化","s":"The teacher tried to simplify the topic of DNA, so she compared it to a recipe book in a kitchen.","t":"老師試著簡化DNA這個主題，所以她把它比喻成廚房裡的食譜書。"},{"w":"anthropomorphism","p":"n.","d":"giving human feelings to animals or objects","c":"擬人化","s":"Saying your dog feels guilty may be anthropomorphism, because it might simply be reacting to your angry voice.","t":"說你的狗感到內疚可能是擬人化，因為牠可能只是對你生氣的聲音做出反應。"},{"w":"immutable","p":"adj.","d":"never changing","c":"不可改變的","s":"Our genes are not completely immutable, because small mutations happen almost every time our cells divide.","t":"我們的基因並非完全不可改變的，因為幾乎每次我們的細胞分裂時都會發生小突變。"},{"w":"inadequate","p":"adj.","d":"not good enough","c":"不足的；不充分的","s":"The cage was inadequate for such a large bird, so the rescue centre moved it to an outdoor area.","t":"那個籠子對這麼大的鳥來說是不足的，所以救援中心把牠移到戶外區域。"},{"w":"inconspicuous","p":"adj.","d":"not easily seen or noticed","c":"不顯眼的","s":"Female ducks are brown and inconspicuous, so they can sit on their nests without being seen by foxes.","t":"雌鴨是褐色而且不顯眼的，所以牠們能坐在巢上而不被狐狸看見。"},{"w":"indistinguishable","p":"adj.","d":"impossible to tell apart","c":"無法區分的","s":"The two species of mosquito are almost indistinguishable, but only one of them carries the disease.","t":"這兩種蚊子幾乎是無法區分的，但只有其中一種會傳播疾病。"},{"w":"irrefutable","p":"adj.","d":"impossible to prove wrong","c":"無可辯駁的","s":"The DNA evidence was irrefutable, so the man finally admitted that he was the child's father.","t":"DNA證據是無可辯駁的，所以那名男子最終承認他是孩子的父親。"},{"w":"misinterpret","p":"v.","d":"to understand something wrongly","c":"誤解","s":"Many people misinterpret a cat's slow blink as sleepiness, but it is actually a friendly sign of trust.","t":"許多人把貓緩慢的眨眼誤解為想睡覺，但它其實是一種表示信任的友善訊號。"},{"w":"misleading","p":"adj.","d":"giving the wrong idea","c":"誤導的","s":"The headline \"Scientists find the gene for intelligence\" was misleading, because hundreds of genes affect how we think.","t":"「科學家找到智力基因」這個標題是誤導的，因為有數百個基因會影響我們如何思考。"},{"w":"observational","p":"adj.","d":"based on watching rather than experiments","c":"觀察性的","s":"Most of her work is observational, so she spends long hours in the forest and rarely does tests in a lab.","t":"她大部分的研究是觀察性的，所以她在森林裡待很長的時間，很少在實驗室做測試。"},{"w":"persuasive","p":"adj.","d":"able to make people believe something","c":"有說服力的","s":"Darwin's arguments were very persuasive, because he supported every idea with hundreds of careful examples.","t":"達爾文的論點非常有說服力，因為他用數百個仔細的例子來支持每一個想法。"},{"w":"predetermined","p":"adj.","d":"decided in advance","c":"預先決定的","s":"Your future is not predetermined by your genes, because choices about food, sleep and exercise also matter.","t":"你的未來並不是由基因預先決定的，因為對飲食、睡眠和運動的選擇也很重要。"},{"w":"provocative","p":"adj.","d":"causing strong reactions or arguments","c":"引起爭議的；挑釁的","s":"The professor asked a provocative question about designer babies, and the class argued about it for the whole hour.","t":"教授問了一個關於訂製嬰兒的引起爭議的問題，而全班為此爭論了整整一個小時。"},{"w":"reproducible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be repeated with the same results","c":"可重複驗證的","s":"Good results should be reproducible, so other labs must get the same answer when they repeat the test.","t":"好的研究結果應該是可重複驗證的，所以其他實驗室重做測試時必須得到相同的答案。"},{"w":"spurious","p":"adj.","d":"false, although it seems true","c":"虛假的；似是而非的","s":"The link between ice cream sales and shark attacks is spurious, because both simply increase in hot weather.","t":"冰淇淋銷量和鯊魚攻擊之間的關聯是似是而非的，因為兩者只是都在炎熱天氣時增加。"},{"w":"unambiguous","p":"adj.","d":"clear, with only one meaning","c":"明確的","s":"The bee's dance sends an unambiguous message, so the other bees fly straight to the right flowers.","t":"蜜蜂的舞蹈傳達出明確的訊息，所以其他蜜蜂會直接飛往正確的花朵。"},{"w":"undisputed","p":"adj.","d":"accepted by everyone","c":"無可爭議的","s":"The lion is the undisputed leader of the group, but younger males may challenge him when he grows old.","t":"這隻獅子是群體中無可爭議的首領，但當他變老時年輕的雄獅可能會挑戰他。"},{"w":"unsubstantiated","p":"adj.","d":"not supported by evidence","c":"未經證實的","s":"The claim that the pill makes children smarter is unsubstantiated, so parents should not waste their money on it.","t":"那種藥丸能讓孩子變聰明的說法是未經證實的，所以父母不應該把錢浪費在上面。"},{"w":"untested","p":"adj.","d":"not yet tried or checked","c":"未經測試的","s":"The new treatment is still untested on humans, so doctors cannot promise that it will be safe.","t":"這種新療法在人類身上仍未經測試，所以醫生無法保證它是安全的。"},{"w":"well-documented","p":"adj.","d":"recorded clearly in many reports","c":"有充分記錄的","s":"The friendship between elephants is well-documented, and many videos show them helping each other in trouble.","t":"大象之間的友誼是有充分記錄的，而許多影片顯示牠們在困境中互相幫助。"},{"w":"continuum","p":"n.","d":"a range where things change gradually","c":"連續體；連續的範圍","s":"Intelligence is not a simple yes or no, because animals lie along a continuum from simple to very clever.","t":"智力並不是簡單的有或沒有，因為動物分布在從簡單到非常聰明的連續的範圍上。"},{"w":"counterexample","p":"n.","d":"an example that shows a rule is not always true","c":"反例","s":"The teacher said all mammals give birth to live young, but a student gave the platypus as a counterexample.","t":"老師說所有哺乳類動物都是胎生的，但一位學生舉出鴨嘴獸作為反例。"},{"w":"experimentation","p":"n.","d":"the process of trying new ideas in tests","c":"實驗","s":"After years of experimentation, the team found a safe way to grow skin in the lab, and burn patients now benefit.","t":"經過多年的實驗，研究團隊找到了在實驗室中安全培養皮膚的方法，而燒燙傷病人如今因此受益。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 6 (observer – gradually)","cards":[{"w":"observer","p":"n.","d":"a person who watches something carefully","c":"觀察者","s":"A careful observer will notice that each crow has a slightly different call, so you can tell them apart.","t":"一位細心的觀察者會注意到每隻烏鴉的叫聲都略有不同，所以你可以分辨牠們。"},{"w":"proposal","p":"n.","d":"a plan or idea that is suggested","c":"提案；提議","s":"The government rejected the proposal to edit the genes of mosquitoes, because many citizens were worried.","t":"政府否決了編輯蚊子基因的提案，因為許多市民感到擔憂。"},{"w":"query","p":"n.","d":"a question","c":"疑問；詢問","s":"If you have a query about your DNA test results, you can email the company, and a genetic adviser will reply.","t":"如果你對DNA檢測結果有疑問，可以寫電子郵件給公司，而一位遺傳顧問會回覆你。"},{"w":"supposition","p":"n.","d":"an idea that is believed without proof","c":"推測；假定","s":"The idea that dinosaurs were grey was only a supposition, but new fossils show that some had colourful feathers.","t":"恐龍是灰色的這個想法只是推測，但新的化石顯示有些恐龍有色彩繽紛的羽毛。"},{"w":"subject","p":"n.","d":"a person or animal used in a study","c":"受試者；研究對象","s":"Each subject in the study wore a sleep tracker, and the scientists compared their results with their genes.","t":"研究中的每位受試者都戴著睡眠追蹤器，而科學家把他們的結果和基因作比較。"},{"w":"fluke","p":"n.","d":"a lucky or unusual result that happens by chance","c":"僥倖；偶然","s":"At first, the scientists thought the clever bird was a fluke, but other birds soon learned the same trick.","t":"起初科學家認為那隻聰明的鳥只是偶然，但其他鳥很快也學會了同樣的把戲。"},{"w":"abnormality","p":"n.","d":"something that is not usual, often a health problem","c":"異常","s":"The scan showed a small abnormality in the baby's heart, but the doctor said it would probably heal by itself.","t":"掃描顯示寶寶的心臟有一個小異常，但醫生說它可能會自行癒合。"},{"w":"agent","p":"n.","d":"something that causes an effect","c":"媒介；作用物","s":"Mosquitoes are the main agent that spreads the disease, so the town cleaned all the standing water.","t":"蚊子是傳播這種疾病的主要媒介，所以這個城鎮清除了所有的積水。"},{"w":"aggression","p":"n.","d":"angry or violent behaviour","c":"攻擊性","s":"Male birds show more aggression in spring, because they must protect their area from other males.","t":"雄鳥在春天表現出更強的攻擊性，因為牠們必須保護自己的地盤不受其他雄鳥侵犯。"},{"w":"behavioural","p":"adj.","d":"relating to how a person or animal acts","c":"行為的","s":"The dog had several behavioural problems, so the family hired a trainer to help it feel calm.","t":"那隻狗有幾個行為的問題，所以這家人請了一位訓練師幫助牠平靜下來。"},{"w":"biologically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way relating to living things","c":"生物學上","s":"Humans are biologically very similar to chimps, but our language and culture make us very different.","t":"人類在生物學上和黑猩猩非常相似，但我們的語言和文化讓我們非常不同。"},{"w":"certainty","p":"n.","d":"the state of being completely sure","c":"確定性；把握","s":"Scientists cannot say with certainty why the dinosaurs had feathers, but warmth and display are likely reasons.","t":"科學家無法確定恐龍為什麼有羽毛，但保暖和展示可能是原因。"},{"w":"commonly","p":"adv.","d":"usually or by many people","c":"普遍地；通常","s":"The fruit fly is commonly used in genetics labs, because it is cheap and breeds every two weeks.","t":"果蠅普遍地被用於遺傳學實驗室，因為牠便宜而且每兩週就繁殖一次。"},{"w":"consciousness","p":"n.","d":"being awake and aware of yourself","c":"意識","s":"Scientists still argue about animal consciousness, but most agree that dogs and apes have feelings.","t":"科學家仍在爭論動物的意識，但大多數人同意狗和猿類有情感。"},{"w":"descriptive","p":"adj.","d":"describing what something is like","c":"描述性的","s":"Her first report was mainly descriptive, so it explained what the monkeys did but not why they did it.","t":"她的第一份報告主要是描述性的，所以它解釋了猴子做了什麼，但沒有解釋為什麼。"},{"w":"detection","p":"n.","d":"the act of finding or noticing something","c":"偵測；發現","s":"Early detection of a genetic disease can help a baby, because doctors can start treatment right away.","t":"遺傳疾病的早期發現能幫助嬰兒，因為醫生可以立即開始治療。"},{"w":"diagnostic","p":"adj.","d":"used to find out what illness someone has","c":"診斷的","s":"The hospital bought new diagnostic equipment, so patients no longer wait weeks for their test results.","t":"醫院購買了新的診斷的設備，所以病人不再需要等好幾週才拿到檢查結果。"},{"w":"effectively","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that works well","c":"有效地","s":"The new drug works effectively against the virus, but it is still too expensive for many patients.","t":"這種新藥能有效地對抗病毒，但對許多病人來說仍然太貴。"},{"w":"efficient","p":"adj.","d":"working well without wasting time or energy","c":"有效率的","s":"Penguins are very efficient swimmers, so they can travel long distances while using little energy.","t":"企鵝是非常有效率的泳者，所以牠們能消耗很少的能量游很長的距離。"},{"w":"entirely","p":"adv.","d":"completely","c":"完全地","s":"Koalas eat almost entirely eucalyptus leaves, so they cannot survive where those trees do not grow.","t":"無尾熊幾乎完全以尤加利樹葉為食，所以牠們無法在沒有這種樹的地方生存。"},{"w":"environmental","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the natural world and surroundings","c":"環境的","s":"Some illnesses come from genes, but others are caused by environmental factors like dirty air.","t":"有些疾病來自基因，但其他疾病是由像髒空氣這樣的環境的因素所造成的。"},{"w":"equally","p":"adv.","d":"to the same degree","c":"同樣地；平等地","s":"The mother and father penguins share the work equally, and they take turns keeping the egg warm.","t":"企鵝爸爸和媽媽平等地分擔工作，而且牠們輪流讓蛋保持溫暖。"},{"w":"existence","p":"n.","d":"the state of being real or alive","c":"存在","s":"Scientists doubted the existence of the giant squid for years, until someone finally filmed one in 2004.","t":"科學家多年來一直懷疑大王魷的存在，直到2004年終於有人拍到了一隻。"},{"w":"fascinating","p":"adj.","d":"extremely interesting","c":"迷人的；極有趣的","s":"The way birds find their way home is fascinating, and scientists are still not sure how they do it.","t":"鳥類找到回家路的方式是極有趣的，而科學家仍然不確定牠們是怎麼做到的。"},{"w":"gradually","p":"adv.","d":"slowly over time","c":"逐漸地","s":"The puppy gradually learned to trust the new family, and after a month it slept happily on the sofa.","t":"那隻小狗逐漸地學會信任新家人，而一個月後牠快樂地睡在沙發上。"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 7 (imprecise – territorial)","cards":[{"w":"imprecise","p":"adj.","d":"not exact","c":"不精確的","s":"Early DNA tests were imprecise, so they sometimes gave the wrong answer about a person's family.","t":"早期的DNA檢測是不精確的，所以有時會對一個人的家族給出錯誤的答案。"},{"w":"ineffective","p":"adj.","d":"not producing the result you want","c":"無效的","s":"The old medicine became ineffective against the germs, so doctors had to find a new one.","t":"舊藥對這些病菌變得無效，所以醫生必須找到新的藥。"},{"w":"instinctive","p":"adj.","d":"done naturally without learning","c":"本能的","s":"Swimming is instinctive for baby ducks, so they follow their mother into the water on their first day.","t":"游泳對小鴨來說是本能的，所以牠們在出生第一天就跟著媽媽下水。"},{"w":"intelligent","p":"adj.","d":"clever and able to learn quickly","c":"聰明的","s":"Octopuses are very intelligent animals, and some have escaped from their tanks by opening the lids.","t":"章魚是非常聰明的動物，而有些章魚曾經打開蓋子從水族箱裡逃脫。"},{"w":"limited","p":"adj.","d":"small in amount or number","c":"有限的","s":"Pandas have a limited diet of bamboo, so they must eat for up to fourteen hours a day.","t":"熊貓只吃竹子，飲食有限，所以牠們一天必須進食長達十四個小時。"},{"w":"misunderstanding","p":"n.","d":"a failure to understand correctly","c":"誤會；誤解","s":"There is a common misunderstanding that humans came from monkeys, but in fact we share an ancestor with them.","t":"有一個常見的誤解是人類是從猴子變來的，但事實上我們和牠們有共同的祖先。"},{"w":"originally","p":"adv.","d":"at first","c":"起初；原本","s":"Dogs were originally wild wolves, but people tamed them and they slowly became our loyal friends.","t":"狗原本是野生的狼，但人們馴服了牠們，而牠們慢慢成為我們忠實的朋友。"},{"w":"permanent","p":"adj.","d":"lasting forever or for a very long time","c":"永久的","s":"Gene therapy may offer a permanent cure, so patients would not need to take medicine every day.","t":"基因療法可能提供永久的治癒，所以病人將不需要每天吃藥。"},{"w":"possibility","p":"n.","d":"something that might happen or be true","c":"可能性","s":"There is a possibility that the gene also affects memory, so the scientists plan to test it next year.","t":"這個基因也有可能性會影響記憶，所以科學家計畫明年進行測試。"},{"w":"potentially","p":"adv.","d":"possibly in the future","c":"潛在地；可能","s":"Gene editing could potentially cure many diseases, but it may also create problems that we cannot yet predict.","t":"基因編輯可能治癒許多疾病，但它也可能造成我們目前還無法預測的問題。"},{"w":"probable","p":"adj.","d":"likely to be true or to happen","c":"很可能的","s":"A cold winter is the most probable cause of the birds' deaths, but scientists are also testing for disease.","t":"寒冷的冬天是這些鳥死亡最可能的原因，但科學家也在檢測是否有疾病。"},{"w":"problematic","p":"adj.","d":"full of difficulties","c":"有問題的；棘手的","s":"Keeping dolphins in small tanks is problematic, because they normally swim long distances every day.","t":"把海豚養在小水族箱裡是有問題的，因為牠們通常每天都游很遠的距離。"},{"w":"purposeful","p":"adj.","d":"done with a clear aim","c":"有目的的","s":"The crow's actions looked purposeful, so the scientists believed it was planning how to get the food.","t":"那隻烏鴉的行為看起來是有目的的，所以科學家相信牠正在計畫如何拿到食物。"},{"w":"rarely","p":"adv.","d":"not often","c":"很少","s":"Male hamsters rarely help raise their babies, so the mother must do all the work alone.","t":"雄倉鼠很少幫忙養育寶寶，所以母倉鼠必須獨自完成所有工作。"},{"w":"reactive","p":"adj.","d":"acting in response to something rather than planning","c":"反應性的；易起反應的","s":"Some dogs are very reactive to noise, and they bark loudly every time a motorbike passes.","t":"有些狗對噪音非常易起反應，每當有機車經過時牠們都會大聲吠叫。"},{"w":"regardless","p":"adv.","d":"without being affected by something","c":"不管；無論如何","s":"The salmon swim upriver regardless of the danger, because they must lay their eggs where they were born.","t":"鮭魚不管危險都會逆流而上，因為牠們必須在自己出生的地方產卵。"},{"w":"responsive","p":"adj.","d":"reacting quickly and positively","c":"反應靈敏的","s":"Babies are very responsive to their mother's voice, and they often stop crying when they hear her.","t":"嬰兒對媽媽的聲音反應非常靈敏，而且他們聽到媽媽的聲音時常常會停止哭泣。"},{"w":"self-evident","p":"adj.","d":"clear without needing proof","c":"不言而喻的","s":"It may seem self-evident that children look like their parents, but the reasons were a mystery until genetics.","t":"孩子長得像父母這件事似乎不言而喻，但在遺傳學出現之前，其中的原因一直是個謎。"},{"w":"situational","p":"adj.","d":"depending on the situation","c":"視情況而定的","s":"The monkey's behaviour was situational, because it acted bravely with friends but hid when it was alone.","t":"那隻猴子的行為是視情況而定的，因為牠和朋友在一起時很勇敢，但獨自一隻時就躲起來。"},{"w":"socially","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that relates to living in groups","c":"社交上","s":"Wolves are socially complex animals, so a lonely wolf often tries hard to find or form a new pack.","t":"狼在社交上是複雜的動物，所以一隻孤狼常常會努力尋找或組成新的狼群。"},{"w":"suitable","p":"adj.","d":"right for a purpose","c":"合適的","s":"The beach was no longer suitable for nesting, because hotels had been built along the sand.","t":"這片海灘已不再適合築巢，因為沙灘沿岸已經蓋了飯店。"},{"w":"supportive","p":"adj.","d":"giving help and encouragement","c":"支持的","s":"Elephants are very supportive of each other, and they gently touch a stressed friend with their trunks.","t":"大象之間非常支持彼此，而牠們會用象鼻輕輕觸碰感到緊張的同伴。"},{"w":"surprisingly","p":"adv.","d":"in an unexpected way","c":"令人驚訝地","s":"Pigs are surprisingly clever, and some can learn to play simple video games with a joystick.","t":"豬令人驚訝地聰明，而有些豬能學會用搖桿玩簡單的電玩遊戲。"},{"w":"systemic","p":"adj.","d":"affecting the whole body or system","c":"全身性的；系統性的","s":"The infection became systemic, so it spread through the patient's blood and needed stronger treatment.","t":"感染變成了全身性的，所以它擴散到病人的血液中，需要更強的治療。"},{"w":"territorial","p":"adj.","d":"defending an area from others","c":"有領域性的","s":"Robins are very territorial birds, and they will even attack their own reflection in a window.","t":"知更鳥是非常有領域性的鳥類，而牠們甚至會攻擊自己在窗戶上的倒影。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 8 (uncommon – harmless)","cards":[{"w":"uncommon","p":"adj.","d":"not happening often","c":"不常見的","s":"White tigers are uncommon in the wild, because they need a rare gene from both parents.","t":"白老虎在野外是不常見的，因為牠們需要從父母雙方都得到一個罕見的基因。"},{"w":"unexpected","p":"adj.","d":"surprising and not planned","c":"出乎意料的","s":"The results were unexpected, because the \"lazy\" ants actually acted as a back-up team when others were lost.","t":"結果是出乎意料的，因為那些「懶惰」的螞蟻在其他螞蟻消失時其實擔任了後備隊伍。"},{"w":"unexplained","p":"adj.","d":"without a known reason","c":"無法解釋的","s":"Some whales beach themselves for unexplained reasons, and scientists are studying whether noise may be the cause.","t":"有些鯨魚因為無法解釋的原因擱淺，而科學家正在研究噪音是否可能是原因。"},{"w":"unusual","p":"adj.","d":"different from what is normal","c":"不尋常的","s":"It is unusual for a male fish to carry eggs, but male seahorses carry their babies in a special pouch.","t":"雄魚攜帶卵是不尋常的，但雄海馬會把寶寶放在一個特別的育兒袋裡。"},{"w":"valuable","p":"adj.","d":"very useful or important","c":"有價值的；寶貴的","s":"Old museum specimens are valuable to scientists, because their DNA shows how species have changed.","t":"博物館的舊標本對科學家很寶貴，因為它們的DNA顯示了物種是如何改變的。"},{"w":"antagonistic","p":"adj.","d":"showing strong opposition","c":"敵對的","s":"The two male cats were antagonistic towards each other, so the owner kept them in separate rooms.","t":"那兩隻公貓彼此敵對，所以主人把牠們分開養在不同的房間。"},{"w":"attuned","p":"adj.","d":"able to understand and react to something","c":"適應的；熟悉的","s":"Dogs are closely attuned to human faces, and they can often tell when their owner is sad.","t":"狗對人類的臉部表情非常熟悉，而且牠們常常能察覺主人什麼時候難過。"},{"w":"deleterious","p":"adj.","d":"causing harm","c":"有害的","s":"Most mutations are deleterious or have no effect, but a few help the animal survive.","t":"大多數突變是有害的或沒有影響，但少數會幫助動物生存。"},{"w":"docile","p":"adj.","d":"calm and easy to control","c":"溫馴的","s":"Farm animals became more docile over many generations, because farmers kept the calmest ones for breeding.","t":"農場動物經過許多世代變得更溫馴，因為農民保留最溫和的個體來繁殖。"},{"w":"emblematic","p":"adj.","d":"being a typical symbol of something","c":"象徵性的；具代表性的","s":"The panda is emblematic of animal protection, and its picture appears on many conservation posters.","t":"熊貓是動物保護的象徵，而牠的圖片出現在許多保育海報上。"},{"w":"gregarious","p":"adj.","d":"liking to be with others","c":"群居的；愛交際的","s":"Sheep are gregarious animals, so a sheep that is kept alone often becomes stressed and stops eating.","t":"羊是群居的動物，所以被單獨飼養的羊常常會感到壓力並停止進食。"},{"w":"intractable","p":"adj.","d":"very difficult to solve or control","c":"棘手的；難處理的","s":"The problem of rats on the island seemed intractable, but a careful plan finally removed them all.","t":"島上的鼠患問題似乎很棘手，但一項周密的計畫最終把牠們全部清除了。"},{"w":"placid","p":"adj.","d":"calm and not easily upset","c":"平靜的；溫和的","s":"The old horse was placid and gentle, so the riding school used it for young children.","t":"那匹老馬溫和而溫順，所以騎馬學校讓牠給年幼的孩子騎。"},{"w":"proclivity","p":"n.","d":"a natural tendency to do something","c":"傾向；癖好","s":"Border collies have a strong proclivity for herding, and they may even try to gather children together.","t":"邊境牧羊犬有強烈的放牧傾向，而牠們甚至可能會試圖把孩子們聚集在一起。"},{"w":"reclusive","p":"adj.","d":"avoiding others and living alone","c":"隱居的；不喜交際的","s":"The snow leopard is a reclusive animal, so few people have ever seen one in the wild.","t":"雪豹是一種不喜交際的動物，所以很少有人曾在野外看過牠。"},{"w":"serendipity","p":"n.","d":"finding something good by chance","c":"意外的好運；機緣巧合","s":"Many great discoveries came from serendipity, because scientists noticed something strange and decided to study it.","t":"許多偉大的發現來自機緣巧合，因為科學家注意到奇怪的事情並決定研究它。"},{"w":"submissive","p":"adj.","d":"willing to obey others","c":"順從的","s":"The young wolf showed submissive behaviour by lying on its back, and the leader stopped growling.","t":"那隻年輕的狼仰躺著表現出順從的行為，而首領就停止了低吼。"},{"w":"timid","p":"adj.","d":"shy and easily frightened","c":"膽小的","s":"The rescued dog was timid at first, but it slowly became braver with daily walks and kind words.","t":"那隻被救援的狗起初很膽小，但隨著每天散步和溫柔的話語，牠慢慢變得勇敢。"},{"w":"observant","p":"adj.","d":"good at noticing things","c":"觀察力敏銳的","s":"An observant student noticed that the ants always took the same path, so she drew a map of their route.","t":"一位觀察力敏銳的學生注意到螞蟻總是走同一條路，所以她畫了一張牠們路線的地圖。"},{"w":"alert","p":"adj.","d":"quick to notice danger","c":"警覺的","s":"Deer stay alert while they eat, and they lift their heads every few seconds to listen for wolves.","t":"鹿在進食時保持警覺，而且牠們每隔幾秒就抬起頭來聆聽狼的動靜。"},{"w":"defensive","p":"adj.","d":"protecting yourself from attack","c":"防禦性的","s":"The mother bear became defensive when we walked near her cubs, so the guide told us to back away slowly.","t":"當我們走近她的小熊時，母熊變得具防禦性，所以導遊要我們慢慢後退。"},{"w":"nimble","p":"adj.","d":"able to move quickly and lightly","c":"敏捷的","s":"Mountain goats are very nimble climbers, and they can stand on rocks that look too small for their feet.","t":"山羊是非常敏捷的攀爬者，而且牠們能站在看起來比牠們的蹄還小的岩石上。"},{"w":"showy","p":"adj.","d":"bright and designed to attract attention","c":"華麗的；引人注目的","s":"The male bird has showy feathers, while the female is plain brown so she can hide on the nest.","t":"雄鳥有華麗的羽毛，而雌鳥是樸素的褐色，好讓她能躲在巢裡。"},{"w":"risky","p":"adj.","d":"possibly dangerous","c":"有風險的","s":"Leaving the group is risky for a young zebra, because lions often attack animals that are alone.","t":"離開群體對年輕的斑馬來說是有風險的，因為獅子常常攻擊落單的動物。"},{"w":"harmless","p":"adj.","d":"not able to cause harm","c":"無害的","s":"Most spiders in Taiwan are harmless to people, but many children are still afraid of them.","t":"台灣大多數蜘蛛對人類是無害的，但許多孩子仍然害怕牠們。"}]},{"unit":16,"theme":"Fixed Phrases & Collocations 固定片語與搭配詞","cards":[{"w":"survival of the fittest","p":"n.phr.","d":"the idea that the best-suited living things survive","c":"適者生存","s":"Some people use \"survival of the fittest\" to describe business, but Darwin meant fitting the environment, not being the strongest.","t":"有些人用「適者生存」來形容商業競爭，但達爾文的意思是適應環境，而不是最強壯。"},{"w":"run in the family","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be common among members of one family","c":"家族遺傳","s":"Musical talent seems to run in the family, because my grandfather, my mother and my brother all play the piano.","t":"音樂天分似乎是家族遺傳，因為我的外公、我媽媽和我哥哥都會彈鋼琴。"},{"w":"birds of a feather flock together","p":"phr.","d":"people who are alike spend time together","c":"物以類聚","s":"Tom and his friends all love insects and spend weekends looking for beetles, so birds of a feather flock together.","t":"湯姆和他的朋友們都熱愛昆蟲，週末都在找甲蟲，所以真是物以類聚。"},{"w":"like father, like son","p":"phr.","d":"a son is often similar to his father","c":"有其父必有其子","s":"My dad laughs exactly the way my brother does, and my grandmother always smiles and says, \"like father, like son.\"","t":"我爸爸笑起來跟我哥哥一模一樣，而我奶奶總是微笑著說：「有其父必有其子。」"},{"w":"the apple doesn't fall far from the tree","p":"phr.","d":"children are often like their parents","c":"有其父母必有其子女","s":"Her mother was a famous scientist, and now she is studying genes too, so the apple doesn't fall far from the tree.","t":"她的母親是一位著名的科學家，而現在她也在研究基因，所以真是有其父母必有其子女。"},{"w":"a chip off the old block","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who is very similar to a parent","c":"酷似父母的孩子","s":"Kevin is as funny and talkative as his father, and everyone at the party said he was a chip off the old block.","t":"凱文和他爸爸一樣風趣又健談，而派對上每個人都說他酷似他爸爸。"},{"w":"in one's genes","p":"adj.phr.","d":"natural to someone because of their family","c":"天生的；與生俱來的","s":"Running seems to be in one's genes, because her parents were both Olympic athletes and she won her first race at six.","t":"跑步似乎是她與生俱來的能力，因為她的父母都是奧運選手，而她六歲就贏得了第一場比賽。"},{"w":"pass on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give something to children or the next generation","c":"傳給；遺傳給","s":"Parents can pass on certain illnesses to their children, so doctors sometimes suggest a gene test before pregnancy.","t":"父母可能會把某些疾病遺傳給孩子，所以醫生有時會建議在懷孕前做基因檢測。"},{"w":"take after","p":"v.phr.","d":"to look or behave like an older family member","c":"長得像；性格像（長輩）","s":"I take after my grandmother, because we both have green eyes and we both love gardening.","t":"我長得像我奶奶，因為我們都有綠色的眼睛，而且都熱愛園藝。"},{"w":"the early bird catches the worm","p":"phr.","d":"people who start early will succeed","c":"早起的鳥兒有蟲吃","s":"My mum always wakes me at six before exams, because she believes the early bird catches the worm.","t":"考試前我媽媽總是六點叫我起床，因為她相信早起的鳥兒有蟲吃。"},{"w":"a leopard can't change its spots","p":"phr.","d":"people cannot change their basic character","c":"本性難移","s":"He promised to stop being late, but he was late again the next day, so a leopard can't change its spots.","t":"他答應不再遲到，但隔天又遲到了，所以真是本性難移。"},{"w":"cry wolf","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give a false warning so people stop believing you","c":"謊報危險；放羊的孩子","s":"If you cry wolf too often about being sick, your teacher may not believe you when you really feel ill.","t":"如果你太常謊報生病，當你真的不舒服時老師可能不會相信你。"},{"w":"let the cat out of the bag","p":"v.phr.","d":"to tell a secret by mistake","c":"洩露祕密","s":"We planned a surprise party for Mum, but my little sister let the cat out of the bag, so the surprise was ruined.","t":"我們為媽媽計畫了一場驚喜派對，但我妹妹洩露了祕密，所以驚喜就泡湯了。"},{"w":"the black sheep of the family","p":"n.phr.","d":"a family member who is different or disapproved of","c":"家族中的害群之馬；異類","s":"Everyone in my family became a doctor, but my uncle became a rock singer, so he calls himself the black sheep of the family.","t":"我家每個人都成了醫生，但我叔叔成了搖滾歌手，所以他自稱是家族中的異類。"},{"w":"the lion's share","p":"n.phr.","d":"the largest part of something","c":"最大的一份","s":"The dominant wolf usually takes the lion's share of the food, while the younger wolves wait for what is left.","t":"地位最高的狼通常拿走食物中最大的一份，而年輕的狼則等著吃剩下的。"},{"w":"you can't teach an old dog new tricks","p":"phr.","d":"it is hard to change old habits","c":"老狗學不會新把戲；積習難改","s":"My grandfather refuses to use a smartphone and says you can't teach an old dog new tricks, but I am still trying to teach him.","t":"我爺爺拒絕使用智慧型手機，還說老狗學不會新把戲，但我仍在努力教他。"},{"w":"monkey see, monkey do","p":"phr.","d":"people copy what others do without thinking","c":"有樣學樣","s":"My little brother copies everything I do, so when I started eating vegetables, he did too—monkey see, monkey do.","t":"我弟弟什麼都學我，所以當我開始吃蔬菜時，他也跟著吃——真是有樣學樣。"},{"w":"dog-eat-dog","p":"adj.","d":"very competitive, where people harm others to succeed","c":"殘酷競爭的；弱肉強食的","s":"Life in the wild is a dog-eat-dog world, and only the animals that find enough food survive the winter.","t":"野外的生活是一個弱肉強食的世界，而只有找到足夠食物的動物才能熬過冬天。"},{"w":"give rise to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to cause something to happen or exist","c":"引起；導致","s":"A small change in one gene can give rise to a new feature, and over time that feature may spread through the species.","t":"一個基因的小改變就能導致一個新特徵的出現，而隨著時間推移，這個特徵可能會擴散到整個物種。"},{"w":"ruffle someone's feathers","p":"v.phr.","d":"to annoy or upset someone","c":"惹惱某人","s":"My classmate's rude joke about my drawing ruffle someone's feathers, but I tried to stay calm and smiled at him.","t":"我同學對我畫作的無禮玩笑惹惱了我，但我試著保持冷靜並對他微笑。"}]}];
